    "ogHeadline": "CHAINSAW MAN\nASSASSINS ARC INCOMING",
    "ogAccent": "B5179E",
    "body": "MAPPA turned its **15th anniversary presentation on June 19** into a Chainsaw Man moment. The studio dropped a first teaser for the next anime chapter — the **\"International Assassins Arc\"** — and didn't stop at the show. A new Chainsaw Man mobile game and an original opening animation movie came in the same breath.\n\nThe take: Chainsaw Man isn't a hit they're managing, it's a franchise they're expanding. When a studio rolls out an arc teaser, a game, and a standalone animation piece all at once, that's not a tease — that's a flag planted.\n\n## The Assassins Arc gets its first look\n\nThe teaser is the headline. The **International Assassins Arc** is one of the manga's most-anticipated stretches, and MAPPA finally put moving images on it. No full trailer, no locked window yet — but a first official look is the difference between \"it's coming\" and \"it's real.\" For a series this big, the teaser alone moves timelines.\n\n## A mobile game widens the door\n\nMAPPA also revealed a **Chainsaw Man mobile game**. Anime-to-mobile is how a franchise reaches the people who don't watch every episode but will tap an app on the train. It's a reach play — meeting the audience where the phone already is — and it tells you how confident they are in the IP's pull beyond the core fanbase.\n\n## An original opening movie, because why not\n\nThe studio went a step further with an **original opening animation movie** for the title. That's a flex. Spending real animation budget on a standalone OP piece is the kind of thing only a studio sitting on a sure thing does. It's fan service with a purpose: keep the hype machine warm between arcs.\n\n## Why this clears the bar\n\nThe show only runs big-name anime, and Chainsaw Man is exactly that — one of the few recent titles that crossed fully into the American mainstream. MAPPA stacking an arc teaser, a game, and a movie on its anniversary date is a major-title move, and the 25-to-45 crowd that grew up watching anime go from niche to everywhere is locked in on this one. Watch the teaser, then go back and run the manga before the arc lands.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Jujutsu Kaisen, Attack on Titan and Chainsaw Man Set for New Reveals — CBR](https://www.cbr.com/jujutsu-kaisen-attack-on-titan-chainsaw-man-mappa-event/)\n- [MAPPA Shares Updates Including Chainsaw Man — Anime Corner](https://animecorner.me/mappa-shares-exciting-updates-for-its-upcoming-projects-including-jujutsu-kaisen-s4-chainsaw-man-special-mv-more/)",
