    "ogHeadline": "JUJUTSU KAISEN\nSEASON 4 TRAILER IS HERE",
    "ogAccent": "B5179E",
    "body": "MAPPA opened its **15th anniversary presentation** with the one a lot of people were waiting on: the **first trailer for Jujutsu Kaisen Season 4.** The series got its earliest moving look of the next season, and the room reacted the way you'd expect for one of the biggest anime on the planet.\n\nThe take: it's a tease, not a date. The trailer confirms the season is in motion, but MAPPA kept the specifics close. Read it as a statement of intent — the machine's running — not a calendar entry.\n\n## The first trailer, finally\n\nSeason 4 had already been announced, so the news isn't *if* — it's the first footage. That matters. A trailer is the moment a project stops being a press-release line and starts being a thing you can see. For a fanbase this size, the first images set the whole conversation for the months ahead.\n\n## Still pointing at 2027\n\nThe release continues to read **2027**, and information stays limited. No episode count locked in public, no firm window. That's normal for a MAPPA tentpole this far out — they show you something to hold the room, then go quiet while the work happens. Patience is the price of the polish.\n\n## Why JJK still leads the pillar\n\nJujutsu Kaisen is core mainstream anime — the kind of title that pulls numbers outside the usual fan circles and lands on the same For You pages as the music and the sneakers. A first trailer for its next season is automatically a big-name beat, exactly what this pillar is built for. Watch the trailer, then go re-run the Culling Game in the manga while the wait plays out.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Jujutsu Kaisen Season 4 First Official Major Update — Game Rant](https://gamerant.com/jujutsu-kaisen-season-4-update-june-2026/)\n- [Jujutsu Kaisen Has Exciting News for Fans in June 2026 — ComicBook.com](https://comicbook.com/anime/news/jujutsu-kaisen-has-exciting-news-for-fans-in-june-2026/)",
