    "ogHeadline": "YE SELLS OUT TBILISI\nAS THE WEST SAYS NO",
    "ogAccent": "C8901E",
    "heroCredit": "Rolling Stone",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/ye-kanye-west-tbilisi-georgia-concert-live-nation-israel-1235561670/",
    "body": "Here's the part nobody saw coming. The most cancelled name in music just sold out a 70,000-seat stadium in a single day — in Tbilisi, Georgia.\n\nDinamo Arena moved its full house almost instantly. While promoters in London and France were backing away, a city most of the tour map ignores said come through, and the building filled.\n\n## The West keeps closing doors\n\nWireless Festival in London had Ye penciled for three nights. That fell apart after his visa got pulled. A Marseille date at the Vélodrome got postponed — his call, he says. The pattern's clear: in a lot of Western markets, the booking is the controversy, and the controversy ends the booking.\n\n## And one door opened wide\n\nThe flip side is the headline. Ye lined up dates working with Live Nation Israel — an unlikely partner given everything in his record on that subject. Report it straight: it's a real business arrangement, not a redemption arc, and the tour is routing through markets that'll still take it.\n\nThat's the whole story right now. Western stadiums in publicly funded cities are getting cold feet. Other markets are selling out in a day. The greatest to ever touch a mic, by this host's count, is still the most polarizing name in the building — and the map of where he can actually play is being redrawn in real time.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nWhatever you think of the man, this is a case study in what happens when an artist's brand splits a global audience down the middle. Some cities won't risk it. Others can't print tickets fast enough. Same artist, opposite outcomes, same week.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Rolling Stone — Ye, Live Nation Israel, Tbilisi](https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/ye-kanye-west-tbilisi-georgia-concert-live-nation-israel-1235561670/)\n- [Rolling Stone — Kanye postpones France show](https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/kanye-west-postpones-show-france-ban-1235547343/)\n- [Goal.com — Ye World Tour 2026 dates](https://www.goal.com/en/news/kanye-west-tickets/bltbacc96ac33d87d52)",
