    "heroCredit": "GamesRadar",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.gamesradar.com/games/persona-6-guide/",
    "body": "For the single-player RPG heads, this is the one. Persona 6 got its first official tease at the 2026 Summer Game Fest Xbox showcase. After years of rumors, Atlus finally put it on the screen.\n\nNo release date, no window confirmed — just enough to make it real. The pre-reveal rumor mill had it pegged around 2027, and nothing here moves that up. But the reveal itself is the event.\n\n## Why it's the lead\n\nPersona is the gold standard for the kind of game this show leans toward: deep single-player, big-world, story you live in for a hundred hours. A new mainline Persona doesn't come around often, and when it shows up it instantly becomes the most-anticipated JRPG on the board. The view counts on the reveal coverage tell you the same thing the comment sections do — people have been waiting on this one specifically.\n\nThe series sells a feeling: school year, social links, a double life, a soundtrack that becomes part of your year. P5 turned that into a global phenomenon. P6 is the follow-up to one of the most beloved RPGs of its generation.\n\n## What's next\n\nAtlus moves slow and deliberate. Expect a real gap before gameplay. For now, the reveal is the win — the lane the host lives in just got its biggest name back on the table.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [GamesRadar — Persona 6 guide](https://www.gamesradar.com/games/persona-6-guide/)\n- [GamesRadar — new RPG trailers June 2026](https://www.gamesradar.com/new-rpgs-trailers-june-2026/)\n- [Backyard Drunkard — State of Play / SGF June 2026 roundup](https://backyarddrunkard.com/game-news/state-of-play-june-2026-all-announcements/)",
