    "heroCredit": "PlayStation Blog",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://blog.playstation.com/2026/06/02/first-look-at-god-of-war-laufey/",
    "body": "Santa Monica Studio just did the thing nobody expected: the next God of War isn't about Kratos. It's about Faye — Laufey — his late wife, Atreus' mother. Revealed at the June 2026 State of Play, she gets her own game, her own combat, her own story.\n\nNo release window yet. This is a first look, not a date. But the swing is huge.\n\n## Why it works for this lane\n\nGod of War is single-player, big-world, story-first — exactly the kind of game the host rides for. The 2018 reboot and Ragnarök set a bar most action games still chase. Building a full entry around a character we only knew through other people's memories is the kind of bold choice that either redefines the series or tests it. Either way, you watch.\n\nThe hook is the perspective. We knew Faye as backstory, as the reason for two whole games. Now she's the lead, the afterlife of the gods is her arena, and her combat is built from scratch instead of inherited from Kratos. That's not a spin-off. That's a statement.\n\n## What to watch\n\nSanta Monica won't rush it. Expect a quiet stretch, then a real gameplay reveal down the line. For now, the reveal alone reshaped the conversation about where the franchise goes next.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [PlayStation Blog — first look at God of War Laufey](https://blog.playstation.com/2026/06/02/first-look-at-god-of-war-laufey/)\n- [Pixelkin — State of Play reveals God of War Laufey](https://pixelkin.org/2026/06/03/playstation-state-of-play-june-2026-reveals-new-god-of-war-starring-kratos-wife-laufey/)\n- [PCQuest — State of Play June 2026](https://www.pcquest.com/gaming/state-of-play-june-2026-brings-god-of-war-laufey-and-new-ps-plus-games-trailers-release-dates-and-games-11902607)",
