    "ogAccent": "7A3FF2",
    "heroCredit": "GamingBible",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.gamingbible.com/news/cyberpunk-2077-returns-new-release-night-city-427067-20260617",
    "body": "Edgerunners was supposed to be a one-off. Instead it became the most durable thing in the whole Cyberpunk universe — and this month it shows up somewhere new.\n\n## The crossover\n\nWuthering Waves, the free-to-play open-world action RPG, is collaborating with Cyberpunk: Edgerunners, with the tie-in kicking off in June 2026. A gritty Night City anime dropping into a high-fantasy gacha world sounds like a clash on paper; in practice it's how anime properties travel now — through the games where the audience already lives.\n\n## Why Edgerunners won't die\n\nThe series is the spin-off that did what the game's launch couldn't: it made people fall in love with Night City. Studio Trigger's animation plus a story that actually stuck the landing turned Edgerunners into the franchise's emotional core. CD Projekt RED noticed — there's a second Edgerunners season in production.\n\n## Anime and games are one market now\n\nThis is the through-line we keep covering: anime, games, and the culture around them aren't separate aisles. An anime built off a video game crosses over into a different video game, and nobody blinks. The fans buying the Edgerunners drop are the same fans grinding Wuthering Waves. Two \"industries,\" one audience.\n\n## What to watch\n\nIf you bounced off Cyberpunk 2077 at launch, Edgerunners is still the easiest way in — ten episodes, no homework. Then the Wuthering Waves event is a low-stakes way to see the world in motion. Season two is the real prize on the horizon.\n\n## Sources\n\n- GamingBible — \"Cyberpunk 2077 Returns With Epic New Release That's Taking Us Back To Night City\": https://www.gamingbible.com/news/cyberpunk-2077-returns-new-release-night-city-427067-20260617\n- Game Modifier — \"Cyberpunk 2077 Edgerunners 2026 Update: Project Orion, Mods & Roadmap\": https://gamemodifier.com/blog/cyberpunk-2077-edgerunners-update-2026",
