    "body": "The show leads on the same name it always does. This time the hook isn't an album or a viral clip - it's a date on the calendar two days out. Ye plays Tampa this weekend, and it's the first time TOUR 2026 touches U.S. soil since the opener.\n\n## The dates\n\nYe is booked for Raymond James Stadium in Tampa on June 26 and June 28. The tour kicked off back on April 1 at SoFi Stadium in Los Angeles and is set to close with two nights at Soldier Field in Chicago on September 3 and 4. Tampa is the U.S. re-entry point after a stretch of overseas dates.\n\n## The run that didn't hold\n\nThe European leg has been a coin-flip city to city. He performed in Istanbul, Arnhem and Tbilisi - then watched authorities pull the plug on others. The June 11 Marseille show, the June 19 Chorzow date in Poland, and a July 18 Reggio Emilia show in Italy all got cancelled by local officials over his past antisemitic remarks. Same artist, same week, opposite outcomes depending on the map.\n\n## What's actually on stage\n\nThe production is built around a giant spherical main stage that projects the Earth and the Moon spinning through the set - he's framed the whole thing around return and revival. Whatever you think of him, the staging is a swing, and the Tampa crowd gets the U.S. first look at it.\n\n## Why we cover it\n\nHost calls him the greatest to ever do it, and the standing rule here is simple: report the Ye news factually, newest first, no endorsement and no spin on the politics. This weekend the news is a stadium date in Florida. We tell you it's happening and let the footage talk.\n\n## Sources\n\n- Goal.com - \"How to get Kanye West 2026 tickets: Ye World Tour\": https://www.goal.com/en/news/kanye-west-tickets/bltbacc96ac33d87d52\n- Wikipedia - \"Ye Live Concert Tour\": https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ye_Live_Concert_Tour\n",
    "goLiveAt": "2026-07-28T17:44:22.582Z"
