    "body": "Battle rap lives on the timeline first, the stage second. Right now URL's Summer Madness 15 card is the thing the culture's watching get built in real time on X — and the name that makes it matter is Geechi Gotti.\n\n## Why Gotti is the anchor\n\nGotti is Compton, Crip-culture personified on the mic, and one of the most consistent performers the modern era's produced. URL — the Black-owned New York league that built the blueprint for what battle rap is today — knows what it has in him. Any Summer Madness card with his name jumps from \"good lineup\" to \"appointment viewing.\" That's pull most rappers with albums don't have.\n\n## The card is still cooking\n\nSM15 is URL's flagship season, and the matchups have been rolling out on the timeline — the kind of slow-drip reveal that keeps the scene buzzing between events. Treat specific opponents as developing until URL locks them; the point right now is the card's weight and who's on it, not a finalized bracket. Watch the official accounts for the confirmations.\n\n## The lane the mainstream sleeps on\n\nThis is the hip-hop the charts ignore. No streaming plaque, no radio push — just pen, breath control and nerve in front of a live crowd, run by a Black-owned league for a Black audience that built it. Gotti's a champion in that world and most casual fans don't even know his name. That's exactly why we put it on the show.\n\n## What to watch\n\nKeep your eyes on URL's X feed as SM15 fills in. When Gotti's matchup gets stamped, the timeline's gonna let you know — loud.\n\n## Sources\n\n- VerseTracker — URL: Ultimate Rap League event index: https://versetracker.com/events/url-ultimate-rap-league-queen-of-the-ring-royalty\n- Rap Grid — Battle Rap News: https://www.rapgrid.com/news\n",
