    "heroCredit": "MusicTech",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://musictech.com/features/interviews/akai-mpc-sample/",
    "body": "The standing GEAR beat ties straight to the beat business, and the box everybody in the producer lane is chasing right now isn't the flagship - it's the cheap one. The Akai MPC Sample broke the internet earlier this year and it still hasn't cooled off.\n\n## What it is\n\nThe MPC Sample is a compact, battery-powered standalone sampler - about 23.6 x 19.4 x 5 cm - built to channel the workflow of the vintage boxes that made the sound: the MPC60 and the MPC3000. Akai revealed it March 24, and it was an instant bestseller. Three months later it's still hard to get hold of anywhere in the world; the latest news is fresh stock finally landing in the EU.\n\n## The specs that matter\n\nIt runs on a rechargeable lithium-ion battery with a built-in speaker and internal mic, so you can sample and finish a loop with nothing else in the room. Inside: a CPU with 2GB of RAM and 8GB of storage, expandable over microSD. Four effects engines, 60 effect types including FlexBeat, 32 stereo voices of polyphony, and a real sequencer for actually building beats. All for $400.\n\n## Why producers won't shut up about it\n\nPrice plus portability is the whole story. The barrier to making a beat used to be a room, an interface, a laptop. This is a battery, a speaker, and MPC bones you can finish ideas on at a bus stop. Lower the door, more kids with ideas and no studio get in. That's always the real job.\n\n## Sources\n\n- MusicTech - \"How Akai's MPC Sample became the most-hyped gear of 2026\": https://musictech.com/features/interviews/akai-mpc-sample/\n- Engadget - \"Akai just released a portable and budget-friendly MPC sampler\": https://www.engadget.com/audio/akai-just-released-a-portable-and-relatively-budget-friendly-mpc-sampler-140047113.html\n- Synth Anatomy - \"Akai MPC Sample: available again in the EU\": https://synthanatomy.com/2026/06/akai-mpc-sample-hardware-sampler-inspired-by-the-mpc60-and-mpc3000.html\n",
