    "heroCreditUrl": "https://comicbook.com/anime/list/10-new-summer-2026-anime-you-need-to-watch-this-july-where-to-find-them/",
    "body": "Big titles only in this pillar, and there's no bigger name on the summer board than this one. Bleach's revival has been building to a finale, and the finale is here.\n\n## The lead\n\nBleach: Thousand-Year Blood War Part 4 - 'The Calamity' - is the most anticipated summer 2026 anime, and it's not close. It's the grand finale of the Thousand-Year Blood War, the four-part arc that brought Bleach back from a decade off the air. After three cours that mostly delivered, the expectations on the closer are sky-high.\n\n## Why the hype is earned\n\nThe TYBW revival is the model for how you bring a sleeping giant back - modern budget, modern direction, the source material finally animated the way the manga readers always pictured it. 'The Calamity' is where the Soul Society arc pays everything off. For a generation that grew up on the original run, this is the ending they were owed.\n\n## How to frame it\n\nThis is the kind of premiere that anchors a whole season. The summer 2026 slate is loaded - dozens of premieres rolling out across July - but the finale of one of the Big Three is the center of gravity everything else schedules around. Watch the simulcast windows as the date firms up.\n\n## Sources\n\n- ComicBook - \"10 New Summer 2026 Anime You Need to Watch This July\": https://comicbook.com/anime/list/10-new-summer-2026-anime-you-need-to-watch-this-july-where-to-find-them/\n- Anime Tiger - \"Most Anticipated Summer 2026 Anime: Top 15 Ranked\": https://animetiger.com/most-anticipated-summer-2026-anime-ranked/\n",
