    "body": "Cyberpunk always gets a beat on this show, placed by medium. This week the news is on the anime side, and it finally moved from 'in production' to a date.\n\n## The news\n\nCD Projekt Red and Studio Trigger have set the first look at Cyberpunk: Edgerunners 2 for June 29. The full Edgerunners panel follows at Anime Expo 2026 on July 3, scheduled for 7:30 PM PT. That's the jump from a press line to actual footage - the thing the anime heads have been waiting on since the sequel was confirmed.\n\n## What it is\n\nEdgerunners 2 is a standalone story out of Night City, Trigger back behind the wheel, landing on Netflix. The first season turned a troubled game launch into one of the most beloved anime of its year and sent players streaming back into Cyberpunk 2077. The sequel doesn't have to ride David and Lucy's story - Night City has a thousand of them.\n\n## The game tie-in\n\nIt's not just a show. Cyberpunk 2077's Update 2.4 - framed as the last numbered drop - carries an Edgerunners 2 mission chain: a new fixer handing out edgerunner gigs, show-inspired cyberware, and a remixed soundtrack drop. The anime and the game keep feeding each other, which is the whole reason this franchise won't die.\n\n## Sources\n\n- Final Weapon - \"Cyberpunk: Edgerunners 2 First Look Releases on June 29\": https://finalweapon.net/2026/06/24/cyberpunk-edgerunners-2-first-look/\n- Screen Rant - \"Cyberpunk 2077 Prequel Gets First Teaser\": https://screenrant.com/cyberpunk-2077-prequel-edgerunners-teasers-july-2026/\n",
