    "ogHeadline": "CLOCKWORK\nREVOLUTION",
    "ogAccent": "B8862E",
    "heroCredit": "GamesRadar+",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.gamesradar.com/new-rpgs-trailers-june-2026/",
    "body": "Every so often a single-player RPG shows up mid-year and quietly eats everybody's free time. June 2026's version is Clockwork Revolution — a steampunk world where messing with the past is the whole point, and it dropped right into the RPG conversation.\n\n## Out now, not \"soon\"\n\nClockwork Revolution released June 5, 2026 on PC, PlayStation 5 and Xbox Series X|S. No long wait, no roadmap — it's playable today. That alone separates it from a calendar stuffed with games that are still trailers and release windows. You can actually go run it.\n\n## The hook that's pulling people in\n\nThe premise is the sell: you put time in the player's hands. Reach into the past, change a decision, then watch the present rewrite around it. In an RPG, a mechanic like that turns choice from a menu prompt into a system you're constantly poking at — what happens if I change THIS? That's catnip for the single-player crowd that lives for consequence.\n\n## The look does heavy lifting\n\nThe vibe is vivid steampunk — brass, gears, a city that feels built rather than dropped in. Aesthetic isn't everything, but in a big-world RPG it's the difference between a place you tolerate and a place you want to live in. Early reactions are leaning on how distinct it looks against the usual fantasy and sci-fi defaults.\n\n## Where it fits\n\nThis is comfort food for the GTA-Fable-Cyberpunk lane — go somewhere fully realized, make choices that bite back, lose a weekend. It snuck up on a loaded June, and that's usually how the keepers arrive.\n\n## Sources\n\n- GamesRadar+ — \"These are the 9 new RPG trailers that made me run to my wishlist this June\": https://www.gamesradar.com/new-rpgs-trailers-june-2026/\n- RPG Site — \"The RPGs of 2026: Every RPG and their release dates\": https://www.rpgsite.net/feature/16349-the-rpgs-2026-every-rpg-their-release-dates\n",
