    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.complex.com/music/a/brendan-frederick/ti-kill-the-king-final-album-explained-tracklist",
    "body": "Most rappers don’t get to pick their last chapter. T.I. just did. ‘Kill The King’ drops June 26 as his twelfth and final studio album, and he’s ending it the way he ran it — on his terms.\n\n## A king putting the crown down\n\nT.I. confirmed at the 2026 Grammys that this is the last one. After this, it’s Hollywood, family, and business. He’s framed the title as a metaphor: kill the king inside, let go of the ego and the old personas, walk into the next thing clean. For a man who built a whole lane calling himself King of the South, naming the goodbye ‘Kill The King’ is the most honest thing he could’ve done.\n\n## The board he picked to go out on\n\nEighteen tracks, Grand Hustle and EMPIRE, and a guest list that reads like a career: Usher, Anderson .Paak, 2 Chainz, Jeezy, T-Pain, Summer Walker, and more. The production names tell you he wanted weight on the last one — Dr. Dre and Pharrell both touched it. The lead single ‘Let Em Know,’ a Pharrell beat from January, already went gold. You don’t pull Dre and Skateboard P for a quiet exit.\n\n## Atlanta’s blueprint\n\nStrip the accolades and the story’s simple: T.I. is one of the architects of how Atlanta took over rap. Trap as a sound, the label-boss model, the crossover records that didn’t sell out the corner — a lot of the South’s last twenty years runs through his playbook. A final album from a builder like that isn’t just a release. It’s a marker.\n\n## The lap after the lap\n\nHe’s not disappearing either. The King Succession Tour kicks off July 8 in Phoenix, with his sons Domani and King Harris opening — the name says it all. The crown’s coming off, but it’s getting handed down, not buried.\n\n## Why it leads the show\n\nA legend ending his run on purpose, today, with Dre and Pharrell behind him — that’s bigger than any single victory-lap record. It’s a man deciding when the story ends instead of letting the game decide for him. Respect that, and play it loud.\n\n## Sources\n\n- Complex — “T.I.’s Final Album ‘Kill The King’: Tracklist, Features & More”: https://www.complex.com/music/a/brendan-frederick/ti-kill-the-king-final-album-explained-tracklist\n- HotNewHipHop — “T.I. Confirms The Release Date For His Final Album”: https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/998761-ti-kill-the-king-release-date\n- Wikipedia — “Kill the King (album)”: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kill_the_King_(album)",
