    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.billboard.com/music/rb-hip-hop/kanye-west-bully-deluxe-edition-don-toliver-kings-video-1236277110/",
    "body": "Ye’s spent a year filling stadiums everywhere but home. That changes this week. He’s back on U.S. soil for two nights in Tampa — and after the year he’s had, just showing up stateside is the headline.\n\n## Two nights at Raymond James\n\nYe plays Raymond James Stadium in Tampa on June 26 and 28. These are his first U.S. performances since the April run at SoFi Stadium in Los Angeles. Stateside dates have been the exception for him lately, not the rule, so a two-night stadium stand at home reads as a statement on its own.\n\n## The tour that wouldn’t stop\n\nThe international calendar keeps rolling after Tampa — Albania and Spain in July, Portugal in August. That’s the through-line of this whole era: locked out of a lot of the West’s festivals and venues over the backlash to his past comments, he kept finding stages anyway, and kept filling them. You don’t have to co-sign the man to report the fact.\n\n## What he’s touring behind\n\nThe shows ride on top of an active run of music. The ‘BULLY’ deluxe landed June 19 with new records, and the album’s visual rollout — including the ‘Kings’ video — kept the project in the conversation through the month. Tampa isn’t a nostalgia stop; it’s a working tour behind a working album.\n\n## Report it straight\n\nThis is the standing Ye slot, and the rule on it doesn’t change: report factually, no endorsement, no spin. The story here is narrow and real — the most divisive artist of the moment is back on home stages for the first time since spring. That’s worth marking without editorializing.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nFor a lot of listeners in the 25–45 lane, Ye is still the artist they measure others against — and watching how, where, and whether he can still tour in America is part of the story now. Tampa is the test. He passed it by selling the building.\n\n## Sources\n\n- Billboard — “Ye Drops ‘Bully’ Deluxe, U.S. Dates & ‘Kings’ Video”: https://www.billboard.com/music/rb-hip-hop/kanye-west-bully-deluxe-edition-don-toliver-kings-video-1236277110/\n- Rolling Stone — “Ye / Kanye West concert coverage, 2026”: https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/ye-kanye-west-tbilisi-georgia-concert-live-nation-israel-1235561670/",
