    "heroCredit": "VerseTracker",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://versetracker.com/battles/ultimate-rap-league",
    "body": "Battle rap doesn’t need a chart to tell you when something’s big. It’s the timeline. And right now the timeline’s locked on one matchup: Murda Mook against Geechi Gotti.\n\n## The legend and the champ\n\nMook is a founding father of the modern art form — the Harlem name a whole generation of battlers studied to learn pace, presence, and how to make a room hang on a line. Geechi Gotti is the present: a three-time Champion of the Year out of Compton who carries the West Coast on his back every time he steps up. Put a pioneer across from the reigning best and you don’t have a battle, you have a measuring stick.\n\n## A Caffeine headliner\n\nThe buzz has it as a Caffeine card — Gotti’s Irving Plaza debut, billed as a headline stop on his run. Whether you’re catching it live or on the stream after, the framing is what matters: this is being built as an event, not a slot on an undercard. The platform’s changed over the years, but the stage is still the stage.\n\n## Why we cover it\n\nBattle rap is hip-hop in its rawest form — no hooks, no beat to hide behind, just pen and nerve. It’s also a corner of the culture that’s mostly Black-owned and barely touched by mainstream coverage. Spotlighting the leagues and the names that move it — URL, the Caffeine cards, the champions casual fans can’t name — is the whole point. This is where the writing still lives.\n\n## Mook the standard\n\nThere’s a reason a Mook appearance still stops the timeline years into his career. When the originators step back in, it’s a reminder of where the bar got set. The young dogs study tape of this man. Watching him share a stage with the era’s champion is the kind of full-circle moment the sport runs on.\n\n## Before you bet the house\n\nOne note for the heads: cards move, dates shift, and battle rap announcements live and die on the league’s own channels. Treat the specifics as developing until the league stamps it — but the weight of the matchup is already real.\n\n## Sources\n\n- VerseTracker — “URL: Ultimate Rap League — All Rap Battles”: https://versetracker.com/battles/ultimate-rap-league\n- Ultimate Rap League (@urltv) on X: https://x.com/urltv",
