    "slug": "cyberpunk-night-city-2045-2026",
    "pillar": "gaming",
    "title": "Cyberpunk Feeds the Lore: ‘Night City 2045’",
    "headline": "Night City Keeps Living While Orion Cooks",
    "subhead": "While Cyberpunk 2 stays years out, the ‘Night City 2045’ sourcebook (out June 17) gives fans 312 pages and 600+ locations to dig into.",
    "description": "The ‘Night City 2045’ Cyberpunk sourcebook brings 312 pages and 600+ locations — fresh lore for the universe while Cyberpunk 2 stays years away from launch.",
    "keywords": [
      "Cyberpunk Night City 2045",
      "Cyberpunk sourcebook 2026",
      "Cyberpunk 2 Project Orion",
      "Cyberpunk RED",
      "Night City lore",
      "Sneakz and Beatz",
      "PHRHX gaming"
    ],
    "ogHeadline": "NIGHT CITY\n2045",
    "ogAccent": "0E7C66",
    "heroCredit": "CBR",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.cbr.com/cyberpunk-2077-official-new-release-june-2026/",
    "body": "Cyberpunk 2 is years away. That’s just the truth. But the universe didn’t go to sleep waiting on it — ‘Night City 2045’ just dropped, and it’s a full meal of lore for anybody who can’t let Night City go.\n\n## A 312-page map of the city\n\n‘Night City 2045’ released June 17 in physical and digital, and it’s dense: 312 pages covering the city’s history, geography, government, and the everyday machinery of how the place runs — over 600 specific locations with new maps. It’s the kind of deep-canon material that turns a setting you’ve played into a place you actually understand. For the lore heads, this is the good stuff.\n\n## Keep the medium straight\n\nOne thing to be clear on: this is the tabletop side of Cyberpunk — the pen-and-paper RPG that the whole franchise grew out of in the first place, long before the video game. So it’s not a new game to boot up; it’s a sourcebook to read and build with. That origin is part of why it carries real weight. The video game adapted this world. The book is the world.\n\n## While Orion stays on the horizon\n\nThe reason this lands now is the gap. Cyberpunk 2, codenamed Project Orion, is still a long road — realistically a 2028-or-later project, with the team scaling up across studios. Rather than leave the fanbase on dry land for years, the universe keeps getting fed through other doors: the anime crossovers, the soundtracks, and now a setting book this detailed. Smart way to keep a world alive between games.\n\n## The standing Cyberpunk beat\n\nCyberpunk gets a beat on this show every episode — that’s the rule, by medium. This week it’s not the sequel and it’s not a patch; it’s the lore itself expanding. Night City didn’t stop living while we wait on Orion. Here’s the map.\n\n## Sources\n\n- CBR — “Cyberpunk 2077 Official Prequel Coming June 2026”: https://www.cbr.com/cyberpunk-2077-official-new-release-june-2026/\n- Cyberpunk.net — official news: https://www.cyberpunk.net/en/news/",
