    "heroCredit": "Crunchyroll",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.crunchyroll.com/news/latest/2026/1/28/demon-slayer-infinity-castle-chainsaw-man-reze-arc-saturn-awards-nominations",
    "body": "MAPPA took the arc everybody was waiting on and put it on the biggest screen possible.\n\n## The drop\nChainsaw Man — The Movie: Reze Arc opens theatrically in Japan in July, with the international rollout following in the fall. Instead of dropping the Reze Arc as a TV season, the studio made it a film — the same play Demon Slayer ran with Infinity Castle, and that one turned into one of the highest-grossing foreign films in U.S. box-office history.\n\n## Why Reze\nIf you read the manga, you know. The Reze Arc is where Chainsaw Man goes from chaotic to genuinely heartbreaking — the bomb girl, the cafe, the choice Denji has to make. It's the run that turned a lot of casual readers into people who'd argue this is the best modern shonen. Putting it in theaters with a movie budget is a statement.\n\n## The awards weight\nThis isn't fringe. Reze Arc is already in the 2026 awards conversation, lined up against Demon Slayer's Infinity Castle for top film honors. Two manga adaptations fighting for Film of the Year says everything about where anime sits in the culture right now.\n\n## What to watch\nJapan first, then the fall international run. If you want it unspoiled, lock your date early — the internet will not be gentle once it's out over there.\n\n## Sources\n- GamesRadar — \"New anime in 2026: the biggest upcoming and ongoing shows\": https://www.gamesradar.com/new-anime-release-dates-upcoming-schedule/\n- CBR — \"Demon Slayer Infinity Castle / Chainsaw Man Film of the Year 2026\": https://www.cbr.com/demon-slayer-infinity-castle-film-of-the-year-2026/\n- Crunchyroll — \"Demon Slayer: Infinity Castle, Chainsaw Man — Reze Arc Saturn Awards\": https://www.crunchyroll.com/news/latest/2026/1/28/demon-slayer-infinity-castle-chainsaw-man-reze-arc-saturn-awards-nominations",
