    "ogHeadline": "FABLE GETS\nA DATE",
    "ogAccent": "047857",
    "heroCredit": "The Outerhaven",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.theouterhaven.net/fable-release-date-confirmed-at-xbox-games-showcase-2026/",
    "body": "Fable's been a promise for years. At the Xbox Games Showcase it stopped being a promise and became a calendar entry.\n\n## A real date, a real plan\nAt the June 7 showcase, Playground's Fable reboot got a story trailer, the full voice cast, fresh gameplay and a concrete date: February 23, 2027, with Premium Edition early access on February 18. After the wait, that's the news — a finish line you can actually see.\n\n## It's not Xbox-only\nHere's the part that turned heads. Fable launches the same day on PS5, Xbox Series X/S and PC, and it's on Game Pass from day one. A flagship Xbox franchise going multiplatform at launch says a lot about where the business is headed. More people get to play it; that's the bottom line.\n\n## The world is the host's lane\nFable is a third-person open-world action RPG — melee, ranged and magic you switch between mid-fight, plus the life-sim stuff Fable's always done: buying houses, owning property, relationships, marriage, reputation that shifts based on how you move. Big world, real choices. That's exactly the kind of single-player game we ride for.\n\n## A villain with weight\nThe centerpiece of the reveal was Isabel, the game's villain, voiced by Hayley Atwell. Casting that caliber for the antagonist tells you Playground is treating the story as the spine, not the side dish.\n\n## Sources\n- The Outerhaven — \"Fable Release Date Confirmed At Xbox Games Showcase 2026\": https://www.theouterhaven.net/fable-release-date-confirmed-at-xbox-games-showcase-2026/\n- Xbox — \"Fable: Available February 23, 2027\": https://www.xbox.com/en-US/games/fable\n- Wikipedia — \"Fable (2026 video game)\": https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fable_(2026_video_game)",
