    "headline": "The Witcher 4 Shows Its Tech Hand",
    "subhead": "CD Projekt Red brought a fresh Witcher 4 demo to Unreal Fest and dug into its animation work — proof the next open-world giant is deep in real production.",
    "description": "CD Projekt Red showed a new Witcher 4 demo at Unreal Fest 2026 and detailed its animation tech. It won't hit in 2026, but the open-world RPG is moving.",
    "keywords": [
      "The Witcher 4",
      "Witcher 4 Unreal Fest 2026",
      "Witcher 4 demo",
      "CD Projekt Red Witcher 4",
      "Witcher 4 release date",
      "Sneakz and Beatz",
      "PHRHX gaming"
    ],
    "ogHeadline": "THE WITCHER 4\nIN MOTION",
    "ogAccent": "0E7490",
    "heroCredit": "PCGamesN",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.pcgamesn.com/the-witcher-4/the-witcher-4-release-date-system-requirements-news-trailer-story-everything-we-know",
    "body": "You don't rush a Witcher game. CDPR knows it, and the latest update is less about a date and more about showing the engine actually runs.\n\n## A new look under the hood\nCD Projekt Red brought a fresh Witcher 4 demo segment to Unreal Fest 2026, the Epic event that ran June 16 to 18, and broke down its animation work on the studio's AnsweRED podcast. It's tech-facing, not a hype trailer — but it's real footage from a game a lot of people quietly wondered about.\n\n## Set expectations: not this year\nStraight talk: The Witcher 4 is not launching in 2026. CDPR has it in full-scale production since late 2024 and is planning a whole new trilogy across roughly six years. So this is a marathon. The Unreal Fest demo is a mile marker, not the finish.\n\n## Why it still matters now\nCiri leading a built-from-scratch Witcher on Unreal Engine 5 is one of the biggest open-world bets in the business. For the single-player crowd, the deep-world fanatics, this is the genre's heavyweight loading up. Watching the tech come together is part of the fun.\n\n## The patient lane\nWe lead with what just happened and why it matters — and what happened is the foundation getting shown off in public. No date to chase yet. Just confirmation the next giant is on its feet and moving. We'll be here when it's ready.\n\n## Sources\n- PCGamesN — \"The Witcher 4 release date, trailer, gameplay, and latest news\": https://www.pcgamesn.com/the-witcher-4/the-witcher-4-release-date-system-requirements-news-trailer-story-everything-we-know\n- GamesRadar+ — \"The Witcher 4: Everything you need to know about CD Projekt Red's RPG\": https://www.gamesradar.com/games/the-witcher/the-witcher-4-guide/\n- 80.lv — \"The Witcher 4 Will Not Launch in 2026, New Trilogy Planned Within Six Years\": https://80.lv/articles/the-witcher-4-will-not-launch-in-2026-with-new-trilogy-planned-within-six-years",
    "publishedAt": "2026-06-27",
