    "headline": "Ye Stretches The Run Coast To Coast",
    "subhead": "The Bully tour adds a July 4 San Antonio date and a two-night Chicago homecoming in September, while the second Tampa show goes on as planned despite a senator's push to pull it.",
    "description": "Ye's 2026 tour adds San Antonio on July 4 and two Chicago homecoming shows in September; the second Tampa date goes on after a cancel push failed.",
    "keywords": [
      "Kanye West tour 2026",
      "Ye San Antonio July 4",
      "Ye Chicago shows 2026",
      "Ye Tampa concert",
      "Bully tour",
      "Sneakz and Beatz",
      "PHRHX hip-hop"
    ],
    "ogHeadline": "YE STRETCHES\nTHE RUN",
    "ogAccent": "111111",
    "heroCredit": "IQ Magazine",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.iqmagazine.com/2026/06/tour-news-kanye-west-adds-us-shows-to-ongoing-run/",
    "body": "The standing Ye slot, and the news isn't the album this time — it's the map. The run just got bigger.\n\n## New US dates on the board\nYe added fresh American stops to the ongoing tour: a July 4 show in San Antonio and two nights back home in Chicago on September 3 and 4. The international leg already runs through Tirana, Madrid, and the Algarve. Putting Independence Day in Texas and a two-night stand in Chicago says he's treating this like a real campaign, not a one-off.\n\n## Tampa goes on\nThe second Tampa show at Raymond James Stadium lands June 28 — tonight — after the late-June dates survived a real effort to kill them. Senator Rick Scott launched a petition demanding the Tampa Sports Authority cancel the concerts over Ye's past remarks. It failed. The shows proceeded.\n\n## The homecoming carries weight\nChicago is the whole origin story — the city, the production roots, the chip on the shoulder. A two-night stand there in September reads like the emotional center of the tour, not just two more tickets. He's been chasing that full-circle moment his whole career.\n\n## Read it straight\nSet the politics and the controversy to the side for a second and look at the schedule: a man who supposedly can't tour is adding stadium dates across two continents. The demand is the story. Whatever you think of him, the building still fills up.\n\n## Sources\n- [IQ Magazine — Kanye West adds US shows to ongoing run](https://www.iqmagazine.com/2026/06/tour-news-kanye-west-adds-us-shows-to-ongoing-run/)\n- [Hollywood Reporter — Ye's Tampa shows go on despite Rick Scott petition](https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/music/music-news/ye-kanye-west-tampa-rick-scott-petition-1236631887/)\n",
