    "heroCredit": "The Steel Yard London",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://thesteelyard.london/event/summer-madness-xv-loaded-lux-vs-nu-jerzey-twork/",
    "body": "Standing battle beat, straight off the timeline. The fresh angle this week isn't a matchup — it's the passport.\n\n## URL goes back to the UK\nSummer Madness 15 is heading to London, URL's first flagship on British soil since Summer Madness 8. The Steel Yard is the venue. For a league built in New York basements and barbershop bravado, planting the biggest event of the year across the Atlantic is a flex about reach, not just a venue change.\n\n## The card is loaded\nLoaded Lux versus Nu Jerzey Twork sits at the top — Lux barely battles, so when he does, the whole community books flights. Shotty Horroh versus Geechi Gotti gives the card a real US-vs-UK angle, with Compton's Geechi carrying the West Coast weight he's carried for years. This isn't a soft international stop. It's the A-card.\n\n## A Black-owned league on a world stage\nThis is the part that matters for us. URL is a Black-owned business taking a Black American art form and headlining a stadium-energy event in another country. Battle rap built its own economy with no major-label oxygen. Watching it export that on its own terms is the mission this show keeps pointing at.\n\n## Why the culture travels\nLondon's always had its own scene, but URL showing up with its marquee names treats the UK like a real market, not a novelty. The bars don't need subtitles. Put Lux in a room anywhere on earth and the room understands exactly what's at stake.\n\n## Sources\n- [The Steel Yard — Summer Madness XV: Loaded Lux vs Nu Jerzey Twork](https://thesteelyard.london/event/summer-madness-xv-loaded-lux-vs-nu-jerzey-twork/)\n- [VerseTracker — Summer Madness 15 (URL)](https://versetracker.com/events/url-ultimate-rap-league-summer-madness-15)\n",
