    "pillar": "hiphop",
    "title": "JID And Metro Lock In 'God Doesn't Like Ugly'",
    "headline": "JID And Metro Run It Back",
    "subhead": "JID confirms the title of his next album with Metro Boomin — a follow-up to the Grammy-nominated 'God Does Like Ugly' — pairing one of rap's sharpest pens with one of its biggest producers again.",
    "description": "JID confirms 'God Doesn't Like Ugly,' his next album with Metro Boomin and a sequel to the Grammy-nominated 'God Does Like Ugly.' Sneakz & Beatz on it.",
    "keywords": [
      "JID new album",
      "God Doesn't Like Ugly",
      "JID Metro Boomin",
      "God Does Like Ugly",
      "JID 2026",
      "Sneakz and Beatz",
      "PHRHX hip-hop"
    ],
    "ogHeadline": "JID AND METRO\nRUN IT BACK",
    "ogAccent": "6A0DAD",
    "heroCredit": "HotNewHipHop",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://hiphopdx.com/news/pusha-t-anticipation-clipse-album-social-media-move/",
    "body": "For range — because the show's mission is loving hip-hop in more places than the charts, and JID is one of the best pens breathing.\n\n## The title's official\nJID confirmed his next album is called 'God Doesn't Like Ugly,' the sequel framing to 2024's Grammy-nominated 'God Does Like Ugly.' Flipping \"does\" to \"doesn't\" is a small move with a big wink — same world, opposite verdict. He's building a body of work with a thesis, not just dropping songs.\n\n## Metro back behind the boards\nPairing JID's technical, breathless flow with Metro Boomin's cinematic production is the kind of match that makes albums sound like events. Metro's catalog can swallow a rapper whole; JID's one of the few who can ride those beats and still out-rap the room. The first one worked. The reunion raises the bar.\n\n## Why the lane matters\nJID came up through Dreamville and never traded his pen for a trend. In a moment where a lot of rap chases the shortest path to a playlist, a lyricist getting blockbuster production without sanding down the bars is a small win for the craft. That's the corner of hip-hop this show keeps the lights on for.\n\n## What to watch\nNo date locked yet, but a confirmed title with Metro attached usually means the rollout's close. Keep an eye on the singles — the gap between JID's verses and the average radio record is where the conversation's gonna live.\n\n## Sources\n- [Grammy.com — Clipse, JID and the 2026 album landscape](https://www.grammy.com/news/clipse-reunion-new-album-everything-we-know/)\n- [Consequence — Most anticipated hip-hop albums of 2026](https://consequence.net/list/most-anticipated-hip-hop-albums-2026/)\n",
