    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.crunchyroll.com/news/latest/2026/4/27/kagurabachi-tv-anime-announced-april-2027-premiere-trailer-visual",
    "body": "A manga that started as an internet meme turned into one of the most anticipated anime on the calendar. The hype is real, and the receipts back it.\n\n## The numbers don't lie\nThe newly announced Kagurabachi anime dropped a trailer that cleared 6 million views in under 24 hours. Through June, the team kept feeding the fire — a Chihiro Rokuhira character trailer, then a June 26 reveal casting Katsuyuki Konishi as Togo Shiba. You don't roll out cast announcements like a fight card unless you know people are watching.\n\n## The studio and the staff\nStudio Cypic — formerly CygamesPictures, now folded fully into CyberAgent — handles production, with Tetsuya Takeuchi directing and Keigo Sasaki (Blue Exorcist) on character designs. Takeuchi's action pedigree matters here; Kagurabachi lives and dies on sword choreography, and they hired a battle-animation specialist to draw it.\n\n## Premiere and the AX moment\nThe series premieres April 2027 and streams worldwide on Crunchyroll outside select Asian territories. Before that, it gets a world-premiere spotlight at Anime Expo this July — the kind of convention launch usually reserved for proven franchises, not a manga this young.\n\n## Why it caught fire\nKagurabachi rode a wave of irony into genuine respect — readers came to laugh and stayed because the storytelling and the blade-work are actually that sharp. The anime is the test: get the action right and it's a flagship. The trailer views say the audience already showed up early.\n\n## Sources\n- [Crunchyroll — Kagurabachi TV anime announced, April 2027 premiere](https://www.crunchyroll.com/news/latest/2026/4/27/kagurabachi-tv-anime-announced-april-2027-premiere-trailer-visual)\n- [Anime Corner — Kagurabachi trailer exceeds 6M views in 24 hours](https://animecorner.me/kagurabachi-anime-trailer-exceeds-6-million-views-in-under-24-hours/)\n",
