    "heroCreditUrl": "https://animecorner.me/magic-knight-rayearth-2026-anime-remake-reveals-new-main-cast-and-staff-first-trailer-october-release-date/",
    "body": "Before isekai was a flooded genre, Magic Knight Rayearth helped invent the blueprint. Thirty-one years later, CLAMP's classic is coming back built for now.\n\n## The reboot is real\nA new Magic Knight Rayearth anime premieres October 2026, announced as a 30th-anniversary celebration and unveiled with a first trailer and key visual at AnimeJapan 2026 back in March. For fans who grew up on the original, this isn't a spin-off — it's the whole story, re-drawn for a new generation.\n\n## A heavyweight crew\nE&H Production handles animation, with Kadokawa and TMS overseeing, Yui Miura directing, and Satomi Watabe on character designs. The score comes from Yuki Kajiura — the composer behind some of anime's most recognizable music. The new main trio: Ayane Sakura, Rumi Okubo, and Rie Takahashi. That's a serious lineup for a serious legacy.\n\n## The AX premiere\nThe reboot is set for a world-premiere screening at Anime Expo this July, with Rie Takahashi attending. Launching a nostalgia property in front of the LA convention crowd is a smart read — that room is full of the exact people who taped the original off TV.\n\n## Why it hits the 25-to-45 lane\nThis one's aimed right at our audience. The people who loved Rayearth the first time are grown now, and a faithful, big-budget return is the kind of thing that pulls lapsed fans straight back in. Sometimes the freshest thing on the schedule is something that's 31 years old.\n\n## Sources\n- [Anime Corner — Magic Knight Rayearth 2026 reboot, October release](https://animecorner.me/magic-knight-rayearth-2026-anime-remake-reveals-new-main-cast-and-staff-first-trailer-october-release-date/)\n- [Crunchyroll — New Magic Knight Rayearth anime trailer, visual, cast](https://www.crunchyroll.com/news/latest/2026/3/28/new-magic-knight-rayearth-anime-trailer-visual-main-voice-cast-members)\n",
