    "ogHeadline": "FIRE EMBLEM\nSTEALS THE\nSHOWCASE",
    "ogAccent": "9B1B30",
    "heroCredit": "GamesRadar+",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.gamesradar.com/new-rpgs-trailers-june-2026/",
    "body": "Every showcase has a winner. At the June Nintendo Direct, the strategy heads ate first — Fire Emblem took the night.\n\n## The reveal that stuck\nFire Emblem: Fortune's Weave broke cover at the June 2026 Nintendo Direct with a September 2027 launch on Switch 2, and outlets singled it out as the standout of the whole showcase. In a Direct stacked with reveals, a turn-based tactics game cutting through is a real statement about how deep this fanbase runs.\n\n## Why the lane respects it\nFire Emblem is single-player RPG with a chess brain — permadeath, support bonds, terrain you have to actually think about. It's the patient, methodical cousin of the big-world epics this show loves, and it scratches a different itch: every battle is a puzzle you can lose for good. That tension is the whole appeal.\n\n## The Switch 2 push\nGenesis and Fortune's Weave landing in the same window tells you Nintendo is loading the new hardware with prestige single-player RPGs, not just ports and party games. For people who buy a console for the deep solo campaigns, that's the green light to take Switch 2 seriously.\n\n## The wait\nSeptember 2027 is a long runway, so manage expectations — this is a \"wishlist it and check back\" situation, not a this-year buy. But stealing a Direct this early means Nintendo's confident in what they've got cooking.\n\n## Sources\n- [GamesRadar+ — The new RPG trailers that made my June wishlist](https://www.gamesradar.com/new-rpgs-trailers-june-2026/)\n- [GamesRadar+ — June 2026 Nintendo Direct coverage](https://www.gamesradar.com/news/archive/2026/06/)\n",
