    "slug": "cyberpunk-2077-chrome-rush-2026",
    "pillar": "gaming",
    "title": "Cyberpunk Hits The Arcade With Chrome Rush",
    "headline": "Night City Pulls Up To The Arcade",
    "subhead": "While Project Orion stays quiet, CD Projekt's left-field move is Cyberpunk 2077: Chrome Rush — an arcade-only motorcycle racer tearing through Night City, with cabinets shipping in 2026.",
    "description": "Cyberpunk 2077: Chrome Rush is an arcade-only motorcycle racer set in Night City, with cabinets shipping in 2026 while Orion stays quiet. Sneakz & Beatz.",
    "keywords": [
      "Cyberpunk 2077 Chrome Rush",
      "Cyberpunk arcade game",
      "Chrome Rush 2026",
      "Night City racing",
      "Project Orion",
      "CD Projekt Red",
      "Sneakz and Beatz",
      "PHRHX gaming"
    ],
    "ogHeadline": "NIGHT CITY\nHITS THE\nARCADE",
    "ogAccent": "F5D90A",
    "heroCredit": "ScreenRant",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://screenrant.com/cyberpunk-2077-chrome-rush-official-announcement/",
    "body": "Cyberpunk always gets a beat on this show. This week it's the strangest one yet — Night City in a coin-op cabinet.\n\n## The unexpected drop\nCyberpunk 2077: Chrome Rush is an arcade-only racing game, announced in March and shipping cabinets through 2026. It's billed as \"cybernetically enhanced motorcycle racing with a side of combat\" — basically Road Rash in Night City, weapons and bombs included. Of all the directions to take this IP, a physical arcade racer is the one nobody had on the card.\n\n## What's actually in it\nSeven playable characters, including male and female versions of V, eight bike models, and four tracks pulled from locations in the original game. It's pure pick-up-and-play — a coin-op throwback aimed at barcades and arcades, not your living room. That's a deliberate left turn for a studio known for sprawling single-player worlds.\n\n## Orion's still cooking\nFor the people waiting on the real sequel: Project Orion — Cyberpunk 2 — is still in early development at CD Projekt Red North America, and June came and went without major news. Chrome Rush is the side quest that keeps the brand warm while the main game takes its years. Smart business, even if it's not the announcement Orion fans wanted.\n\n## Why we cover it anyway\nIt's not a single-player RPG, but the rule's the rule: Cyberpunk always gets a beat. And there's something fitting about Night City — a world obsessed with neon and excess — ending up in a literal arcade machine. The aesthetic was always built for it.\n\n## Sources\n- [ScreenRant — Cyberpunk 2077: Chrome Rush officially announced](https://screenrant.com/cyberpunk-2077-chrome-rush-official-announcement/)\n- [Game Rant — Cyberpunk 2077: Chrome Rush](https://gamerant.com/cyberpunk-2077-chrome-rush/)\n",
