    "ogHeadline": "US ON.\nWORLD OFF.",
    "ogAccent": "C0392B",
    "heroCredit": "Wikipedia",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ye_Live_Concert_Tour",
    "pillar": "hiphop",
    "body": "Two things are true at once. Ye is on a U.S. stage tonight, July 4, in San Antonio. And his European summer is gone.\n\n## What fell apart\nThe UK revoked his authorization to enter the country, which killed his Wireless Festival headline slot at Finsbury Park (July 10-12) and took the festival down with it. Italy followed — the July 18 date at RCF Arena in Reggio Emilia got cancelled by local authorities. The overseas leg of the Bully tour is basically a list of scratched-off cities now.\n\n## What's still standing\nThe domestic run keeps moving. The July 4 San Antonio show goes on. Earlier US dates went on after petitions to stop them failed. Whatever you think of the man, the pattern is clear: at home the shows sell and happen, abroad the doors keep closing.\n\n## The straight read\nWe cover Ye every episode because the host considers him one of the greatest to ever do it, and because he moves the culture whether you want him to or not. We're not here to spin it either direction. The facts are the story: a global tour that can't leave the country it started in, still selling out the country it's stuck in.\n\nNo product pitch on this one. Just the report.\n\n## Sources\n- [Wikipedia — Ye Live Concert Tour](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ye_Live_Concert_Tour)\n- [Ticketmaster — Ye Tour Dates 2026-2027](https://www.ticketmaster.com/ye-tickets/artist/885590)\n",
