    "slug": "polyend-drums-tr1000-rival-2026",
    "title": "Polyend Drums: A $2,699 Hybrid Coming for the TR-1000",
    "headline": "The Drum-Machine Arms Race Just Got a New Heavyweight",
    "subhead": "Polyend's new Drums packs analog voices, digital synthesis, and sample playback into one box — with an 8-track sequencer aimed straight at Roland's flagship.",
    "description": "Polyend Drums is a $2,699 hybrid analog + digital drum machine with an 8-track sequencer and X/Y morph fader, positioned against the Roland TR-1000. First batch sold out; next ships Nov 2026.",
    "publishedAt": "2026-07-04",
    "keywords": [
      "Polyend Drums",
      "drum machine 2026",
      "Roland TR-1000 rival",
      "hybrid analog digital drum machine",
      "Superbooth 2026",
      "beat making gear",
      "Sneakz and Beatz",
      "PHRHX gear"
    ],
    "ogHeadline": "NEW\nHEAVYWEIGHT",
    "ogAccent": "C0392B",
    "heroCredit": "Synth Anatomy",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://synthanatomy.com/2026/05/polyend-drums-a-hybrid-drum-machine-a-la-tr-1000-from-poland.html",
    "pillar": "hiphop",
    "body": "Every episode we run a gear beat, because the gear is the beat business. This one's for the people building the drum room.\n\n## What it is\nPolyend — the Polish company behind the Tracker and Play — announced Drums, and it's not a pocket toy. It's a hybrid: analog drum voices, digital synthesis, and sample playback in one performance box. Under the hood there's an 8-track sequencer with deep per-track control and generative tools, a control surface built for playing live, an X/Y fader for morphing sounds in real time, and effects arranged in send, insert, and master chains.\n\n## The price and the target\nIt's $2,699. That's not impulse money — that's a decision. And the decision it's forcing is a direct one: this thing is aimed at Roland's TR-1000, the current king of the high-end drum machine. Polyend basically said \"we'll take that fight.\" The first production batch already sold out; the next run is scheduled to ship in November.\n\n## Is it for you\nReal talk — most bedroom producers don't need a $2,700 dedicated drum machine when a good MPC or even a laptop gets records made. But that's not who this is for. This is for the studio that wants a centerpiece, an instrument you build a whole workflow around, hardware you perform on instead of clicking through. For that room, a hybrid that does analog warmth and digital flexibility in one surface is a serious pull.\n\nCheaper tools make beats. Statement tools make studios. This is a statement tool.\n\n## Sources\n- [Synth Anatomy — Polyend Drums, a hybrid drum machine a la TR-1000](https://synthanatomy.com/2026/05/polyend-drums-a-hybrid-drum-machine-a-la-tr-1000-from-poland.html)\n- [MusicTech — Polyend unveils Drums](https://musictech.com/news/gear/polyend-drums/)\n",
