    "ogHeadline": "THE\nCOUNTDOWN",
    "ogAccent": "1E88E5",
    "heroCredit": "GTA BOOM",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.gtaboom.com/when-is-gta-6-trailer-3-coming-the-window-is-clearer-19a0",
    "pillar": "gaming",
    "body": "This show leans single-player RPG and big-world games on purpose. GTA 6 is the biggest big-world game there's ever been, and the machine around it just woke up.\n\n## The marketing switch flipped\nFor over a year, GTA 6 news meant one trailer and a lot of waiting. That's over. Rockstar opened pre-orders on June 25, revealed the cover art, and — importantly for how this show thinks about games — confirmed on June 24 that GTA 6 is a single-player experience first. The full marketing campaign is officially rolling.\n\n## Trailer 3 and the date\nThe next trailer is the one everybody's holding their breath for. The likeliest window is mid-July, possibly timed around the World Cup final, though Rockstar could drop it any moment. For scale: Trailer 2 sits near 165 million YouTube views. Trailer 3 is expected to make that number look small. And Take-Two's CEO reaffirmed the release won't slip again — November 19, 2026 is locked.\n\n## Why it matters here\nGaming picks on this show get ranked by what's actually pulling views, filtered to the host's single-player lane. Nothing on the planet clears that bar like this. A single-player-first open world of this size, with this much anticipation, is the exact tentpole the whole lane is built around.\n\nThe wait's almost math now. Count the days.\n\n## Sources\n- [GTA BOOM — When is GTA 6 Trailer 3 coming](https://www.gtaboom.com/when-is-gta-6-trailer-3-coming-the-window-is-clearer-19a0)\n- [Wikipedia — Grand Theft Auto VI](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grand_Theft_Auto_VI)\n",
