    "body": "Some retros are just colorways. The 'True Blue' 3 is history. It's the shoe tied to the era that made the 3 legendary, and it's back July 18 at $230.\n\n## The detail that matters\nThis run carries the 'Nike Air' branding on the heel — the way the 1988 pair did, before the Jumpman took that spot on later retros. For 3 heads that's the whole conversation. Get the heel right and the OG crowd shows up. Get it wrong and you hear about it for years. Jordan Brand got it right here.\n\nGrey elephant print on the toe and heel, the classic blue accents, white leather. Clean, loud without trying, the kind of pair that goes with everything and still gets stopped in the street.\n\n## Where it sits this month\nJuly's a stacked Jordan month, but the 3 'True Blue' is the one with real weight behind it. A colorway that carries this much story doesn't need a gimmick or a collab to move — it moves on name alone. If you missed the last run, this is the reset.\n\nMark the 18th. This is a first-of-the-month priority, not a maybe.\n\n## Sources\n- [Sneaker Bar Detroit — Air Jordan release dates](https://sneakerbardetroit.com/air-jordan-release-dates/)\n- [House of Heat — Every Air Jordan release in July 2026](https://houseofheat.co/jordan/upcoming-jordan-releases-july-2026)\n- [Complex — July 2026 Air Jordan release dates](https://www.complex.com/sneakers/a/victor-deng/july-2026-air-jordan-release-dates-air-jordan-7-miro)"
