    "pillar": "anime",
    "body": "Ghost in the Shell is one of the pillars — the work that taught a whole generation what anime could be about. So a new adaptation isn't a small thing. And this one drops today, July 7, on Prime Video.\n\n## What's different this time\nIt's hand-drawn. In an era where a lot of big productions lean on CG shortcuts, going hand-drawn is a statement about care. Early reactions single out the visuals and, just as important, the faithfulness — this version reaches back to the original manga instead of remixing the story everybody already argues about.\n\nKing Gnu handles the opening with a track called 'Go Ghost.' That's a real co-sign. King Gnu doesn't attach to throwaway projects, and a strong OP sets the tone before a single line of dialogue lands.\n\n## Why it leads the anime block\nBig name, major title, out today — that's the trifecta. We don't run niche premieres for the sake of it, but Ghost in the Shell is the opposite of niche. It's a franchise that shaped film and games far outside anime, and a faithful hand-drawn take is exactly the kind of return that pulls in both the longtime heads and people who only know the name.\n\nBlock out the evening. This is the one to watch first.\n\n## Sources\n- [Complex — New Anime Release Guide (July 2026)](https://www.complex.com/pop-culture/a/khal/anime-release-guide)\n- [GamesRadar — New anime in 2026](https://www.gamesradar.com/new-anime-release-dates-upcoming-schedule/)\n- [ComicBook — Every anime coming to streaming July 2026](https://comicbook.com/anime/list/every-anime-coming-to-netflix-in-july-2026-including-one-pieces-new-spinoff/)",
