    "body": "There's a short list of anime that defined a generation, and Bleach is on it. Ichigo, the soul reapers, the whole world Tite Kubo built — it raised people. So the fact that it's finally taking its last bow means something. The closing run streams July 25 on Hulu.\n\n## The end of a long road\nThe modern Bleach revival gave the story the animation budget the early run never got, and it's been paying off the ending fans waited more than a decade for. This last stretch is the payoff to the payoff — the final beats of a war that's been building the whole time.\n\n## Why it belongs here\nWe keep the anime block to big names, and few names are bigger. This isn't a small sequel or a spin-off nobody asked for. It's the curtain call on one of the three or four shows that pulled Western audiences into anime in the first place.\n\nIf you fell off somewhere in the middle, the revival era is worth catching up on before this drops — the animation alone makes the rewatch worth it. And if you rode the whole way, July 25 is the day the story you grew up with finally lands its ending. Respect the run.\n\n## Sources\n- [Complex — New Anime Release Guide (July 2026)](https://www.complex.com/pop-culture/a/khal/anime-release-guide)\n- [GamesRadar — New anime in 2026](https://www.gamesradar.com/new-anime-release-dates-upcoming-schedule/)\n- [ComicBook — Every anime coming to streaming July 2026](https://comicbook.com/anime/list/every-anime-coming-to-netflix-in-july-2026-including-one-pieces-new-spinoff/)",
