    "pillar": "anime",
    "body": "Cyberpunk gets a beat every episode, and this week it lives in anime. Edgerunners 2 moved past the tease — there's a full trailer now, a Fall 2026 window on Netflix, and the details that turn a rumor into a real show.\n\n## What's actually new\nLast time we talked, it was a first look out of Anime Expo. Now CD Projekt Red and Trigger have put a release window on it and shown real story. It's a standalone ten-episode arc — you don't need the first season memorized to jump in. New cast, too: Weak, a veteran edgerunner who used to go by 'King'; D, a Snake Nation netrunner running on revenge; and Roman Carax, a young film obsessive chasing real stories through the city's worst corners.\n\n## The music co-sign\nThe first Edgerunners lived and died on its soundtrack — that's part of why it hit so hard outside the usual anime crowd. Round two keeps that going: Rico Nasty cut an original song for it, 'You Can't Run From Me,' written for the show and already streaming everywhere. That's the kind of crossover that pulls hip-hop heads into an anime they might've skipped.\n\n## Why it clears the bar\nWe hold the anime block to big names, and this is one of the biggest cross-media properties going — the show that turned a broken game into a comeback story is running it back with a clean slate. Fall's the window. The trailer's live. The Rico Nasty track is the appetizer.\n\n## Sources\n- [CD PROJEKT RED — Edgerunners 2 new trailer and Fall 2026 window](https://press.cdprojektred.com/en/news/1831/cyberpunk-edgerunners-2-gets-new-trailer-and-fall-2026-release-window)\n- [Worthplaying — Edgerunners 2 scheduled for Fall 2026 on Netflix](https://worthplaying.com/article/2026/6/30/news/150338-cyberpunk-edgerunners-2-scheduled-to-air-on-netflix-in-fall-2026-trailer/)\n- [Cyberpunk: Edgerunners 2 official site](https://www.cyberpunk.net/en/edgerunners2)",
