    "heroCredit": "Collider",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://collider.com/best-anime-netflix-crunchyroll-july-2026/",
    "pillar": "anime",
    "body": "Not every big anime this summer is a sequel. Sparks of Tomorrow is an original, it's from Kyoto Animation, and it's already one of the most talked-about premieres of the season. It dropped July 5 on Netflix and runs weekly from there.\n\n## Why KyoAni is the headline\nWhen Kyoto Animation makes an original, people pay attention — this is the studio with maybe the most recognizable in-house craft in the business, the fluid character work and lighting that make their shows look like nothing else. Pointing that team at a historical fantasy is a real swing, and the early word is the visuals are carrying it exactly like you'd hope.\n\n## The bet on originals\nAdaptations are the safe money — a hit manga comes with a built-in audience. An original has to earn its crowd from scratch. That's what makes Sparks of Tomorrow worth flagging: no source material to lean on, just a studio trusting its own storytelling and its own art. When it works, that's how you get the shows people remember for years.\n\n## The read\nWe don't run niche premieres for the sake of it, but a KyoAni original leading the summer-season conversation isn't niche — it's one of the tentpoles. If you want something with weight behind it that isn't season eight of a franchise you're already ten arcs deep in, start here. It's streaming now.\n\n## Sources\n- [Collider — Best anime coming to Netflix and Crunchyroll in July](https://collider.com/best-anime-netflix-crunchyroll-july-2026/)\n- [OtakuKart — Summer 2026 anime everyone's talking about](https://otakukart.com/13-summer-2026-anime-everyones-actually-talking-about-not-just-the-big-sequels/)\n- [ScreenRant — Most anticipated summer 2026 anime](https://screenrant.com/most-anticipated-summer-2026-anime/)",
