    "ogHeadline": "STILL\nON.",
    "ogAccent": "1E5AA8",
    "heroCredit": "Euronews",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.euronews.com/culture/2026/04/23/italy-under-pressure-over-kanye-ye-west-gig-after-uk-france-poland-and-switzerland-cancell",
    "pillar": "hiphop",
    "body": "We report Ye straight every episode. The last few weeks the story's been cancellations. This one's about what survived.\n\n## What's still on the board\nAfter the UK pulled his entry and France, Poland, Switzerland and then Italy dropped their dates, two European stops are still listed: Madrid on July 30 and the Algarve in Portugal on August 7. Nobody's mounted a campaign to stop those two, and that's turned out to be the deciding factor all summer. The dates that get organized against fall. The quiet ones hold.\n\n## The US never blinked\nBack home it's a different picture. The Alamodome show in San Antonio went ahead over the mayor's objection. In Tampa he brought his daughter North West and Kodak Black out on stage. Politicians asked for cancellations; the venues booked it anyway and the crowds showed up. The gap between the European reception and the American one is the real story here.\n\n## Why the tour exists\nAll of this is the Ye Live Concert Tour, his seventh headlining run, behind the 2026 album Bully. It opened April 1 in Inglewood and has been trailed by controversy tied to his past antisemitic comments the whole way. We're not relitigating that record — it's what it is, and it's why the cancellations keep coming. We're just telling you where the man can actually get on a stage.\n\n## What to watch\nIf Madrid and the Algarve go off clean, that's the template for the rest of the run: book quiet, play fast, don't give anybody a target. If they fall too, the European chapter is basically closed for the year.\n\n## Sources\n- Euronews — Italy under pressure over Ye gig after UK, France, Poland and Switzerland cancelled\n- Wikipedia — Ye Live Concert Tour\n- KENS5 / Tampa Bay Times — San Antonio and Tampa shows",
