    "pillar": "anime",
    "body": "Cyberpunk always gets a beat, and the anime side just moved past the tease. There's a real trailer now, a window, and a hip-hop hook attached.\n\n## The news\nCD Projekt Red dropped a new Edgerunners 2 trailer and set a Fall 2026 release window, exclusively on Netflix. The song in the trailer is an original by Rico Nasty — 'You Can't Run From Me,' written for the show and already streaming everywhere. The first series lived and died on its soundtrack, so leading round two with a purpose-built rap record is the right move.\n\n## What it actually is\nThis is a standalone 10-episode story, not a direct sequel — a different crew and a clean slate in Night City. The center is Weak, a washed-up cyberpunk legend forced to live without chrome and searching for purpose, while a nomad named D chases revenge into corpo secrets. You don't need the first season to jump in.\n\n## Why it's the crossover\nAn original Rico Nasty cut on a marquee anime is exactly the kind of place we like to show hip-hop love — outside the usual chart lanes. Music and animation have carried this franchise from the jump, and CDPR clearly knows it.\n\n## What to watch\nFall usually means October, but the window runs September to November. Watch for a hard date and a full track list — if the soundtrack goes as deep as the first one, that's its own event.\n\n## Sources\n- CD Projekt Red Press Center — Edgerunners 2 new trailer and Fall 2026 window\n- Crunchyroll — Edgerunners 2 release date and visual\n- GamesRadar — Edgerunners season 2 everything we know",
