    "body": "Biggest single-player game on the planet, so it leads the gaming block. The date situation is finally settled.\n\n## The lock\nRockstar has Grand Theft Auto VI down for November 19, 2026, and Take-Two's CEO went on record that it won't be delayed again. After a run of shifting windows, an executive putting his name on 'no more delays' is the update — the calendar is real now.\n\n## The marketing wave\nThe push kicked off at the end of June. Pre-orders opened at midnight on June 25 alongside a cover-art reveal and a confirmed price, and a third trailer is expected in the late-June-to-early-July window. Rockstar is finally turning the machine on.\n\n## The July 14 wrinkle\nGTA Online's next major content update is lined up for around July 14 — likely the last big drop before Rockstar puts everything behind GTA VI. If you still run Online, that's the send-off.\n\n## Why it's a single-player story\nThis is the host's lane exactly: a massive open-world single-player game with a marketing cycle that'll swallow the rest of the year. Everything else in gaming plans around this date now.\n\n## What to watch\nTrailer 3 is the next domino — watch for it to land before the July 14 Online update, and watch pre-order tiers for the edition breakdown.\n\n## Sources\n- Rockstar Games Newswire — GTA VI release date\n- Vice — Take-Two CEO confirms GTA 6 won't be delayed again\n- GTA BOOM — why Trailer 3 could come before the July 14 Online DLC",
