    "pillar": "gaming",
    "body": "Cyberpunk always gets a beat, and the game-side news this week is the franchise stepping into somebody else's arena.\n\n## The crossover\nCyberpunk is coming to Apex Legends on July 14, bringing a Night City E-District takeover and a set of Cyberpunk-themed skins. It's a reach outside the single-player game, but it keeps the aesthetic in front of a completely different, massive player base — smart for a title that's spent 2026 in a full victory lap.\n\n## The bigger run\nThe context is a game that's still climbing: Cyberpunk 2077 crossed 40 million copies sold as of early July. That's the comeback nobody saw coming after launch, and CDPR is cashing it in — the crossover sits alongside new merch like a 1:1 Thermal Katana replica and a tabletop card game returning the IP to its roots.\n\n## Why we keep covering it\nThe rule's the rule — Cyberpunk gets a slot every episode — but it earns it right now. This is a franchise in its strongest stretch ever, spreading into games, anime and physical goods at the same time.\n\n## What to watch\nWatch how long the Apex event runs and whether the skins carry Night City characters. And keep an eye on Orion — the next mainline game is the real prize behind all this brand-keeping.\n\n## Sources\n- cyberpunk.net — Cyberpunk is coming to Apex Legends\n- Game Rant — new official Cyberpunk 2077 release confirmed for July 14\n- ScreenRant — Cyberpunk 2077 July 2026 sales update",
