    "ogHeadline": "66\nDAYS.",
    "ogAccent": "6B2233",
    "heroCredit": "Wikipedia",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phantom_Blade_Zero",
    "pillar": "gaming",
    "body": "Single-player RPG lane, host's exact taste. One of the most stylish action games on the calendar just moved its date.\n\n## The delay\nPhantom Blade Zero is now set for October 29, 2026 on PS5 and PC, pushed back from September 9. A late slip on a game this ambitious usually means the team wants the extra runway to land the combat — and combat is the whole pitch here.\n\n## What it is\nThis is a single-player wuxia action RPG built in Unreal Engine 5, blending martial arts with machinery in a style the developer calls 'Kungfupunk.' You play Soul, an elite assassin who carries two primary and two secondary weapons, with blocking, parrying and dodging against color-telegraphed enemy attacks.\n\n## The hook in the story\nSoul gets framed for the murder of The Order's patriarch and nearly killed in the manhunt. A mystic healer saves him, but the fix only holds for 66 days — a hard clock that hangs over the whole run. That structure is what sets it apart from the usual soulslike.\n\n## Why it's here\nFast, single-player, hand-crafted, story on a timer — that's the lane exactly. The delay to late October also clears it of a crowded September, which helps it stand out.\n\n## What to watch\nWatch for a fresh combat deep dive before launch and whether the 66-day clock is strict or flexible — that one design choice will decide how the game actually plays.\n\n## Sources\n- Wikipedia — Phantom Blade Zero\n- GameWatcher — Phantom Blade Zero release date, gameplay, trailers",
