    "heroCreditUrl": "https://versetracker.com/events/url-ultimate-rap-league-summer-madness-15",
    "body": "Battle rap builds its biggest nights one matchup at a time, and URL — the Ultimate Rap League, the sport's biggest Black-owned platform — just added another heavy one to Summer Madness XV.\n\n## The new bout\nURL announced Geechi Gotti vs Shotty Horroh as the fourth matchup for Summer Madness XV, set for September 21 in London. It joins the already-announced headliner, Loaded Lux vs Nu Jerzey Twork, on a card that's filling out fast.\n\n## Why Gotti on the marquee matters\nGeechi Gotti is Compton to the core and one of the most decorated pens of his era — a former URL Champion of the Year who built his name on consistency, not one-off moments. When URL puts him on a card this size, they're telling you the night is meant to be judged bar for bar.\n\n## The bigger picture\nThis is the part of hip-hop the charts skip — a Black-owned league drawing thousands to a room to watch writing get judged live, no beat, no hook, just pens. Summer Madness is URL's flagship, and stacking it with names like Lux, Twork and Gotti keeps the sport's center of gravity exactly where it's always been.\n\n## What we're watching\nOne card, marquee names, and the whole calendar bending around it. That's the pull of Summer Madness — when the dates get locked, the culture clears the weekend. We'll keep the light on the leagues doing it for the love and the craft.\n\n## Sources\n- VerseTracker — Summer Madness XV event page: https://versetracker.com/events/url-ultimate-rap-league-summer-madness-15\n- Ultimate Rap League — official battles: https://urltv.tv/battles\n- VerseTracker — Geechi Gotti profile: https://versetracker.com/rapper/geechi-gotti\n\nBuilt for the culture. Operated from San Diego. Run by PHRHX through Sneakz & Beatz LLC. Black-owned, four pillars: sneakers, hip-hop, anime, gaming.",
