    "headline": "She Held\nThe Ring.",
    "subhead": "Sparky D answered Roxanne Shanté in the 1985 Roxanne Wars and helped prove a woman could battle bar for bar. She has died at 61.",
    "description": "Sparky D, the Brownsville MC who answered Roxanne Shanté in the 1985 Roxanne Wars with a gold single, has died at 61. A tribute to a battle-rap pioneer.",
    "keywords": [
      "Sparky D",
      "Roxanne Wars",
      "Doreen Broadnax",
      "female battle rapper",
      "Sparky's Turn",
      "hip-hop pioneer",
      "Sneakz and Beatz hip-hop",
      "PHRHX"
    ],
    "ogHeadline": "She held\nthe ring.",
    "ogAccent": "3A3A3A",
    "heroCredit": "Complex",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.complex.com/music/a/markelibert/mc-sparky-d-roxanne-wars-icon-dies",
    "body": "Some names built the room the rest of us stand in. Sparky D was one of them. Doreen Broadnax died on July 4, 2026, at 61, and hip-hop lost one of the first women to ever pick up the mic and battle.\n\n## The record that made history\nWhen Roxanne Shanté lit the fuse in the Roxanne Wars, Sparky D answered with 'Sparky's Turn (Roxanne, You're Through)' in 1985. The single reportedly sold more than 300,000 copies within days and later went gold — proof, on wax, that a woman could stand in the exchange and hold her own bar for bar.\n\n## Brownsville roots, a real catalog\nShe came out of Brooklyn and worked with a generation of pioneers — Spyder D, Roxanne Shanté, Kool DJ Red Alert and more. In 1988 she released a full-length, 'This Is Sparky D's World,' on B-Boy Records. She was in the rooms where the culture's earliest battle language got written.\n\n## A second act in faith\nHer later life wasn't a straight line, and she was open about the hard parts. She found her footing again in Christianity, moved to Atlanta, founded Treasure Ministries and turned toward gospel — winning a Gospel Choice Award in 2007. She kept building, just on a different stage.\n\n## Why we lead the show with this\nThe PHRHX Show lives on battle rap, and the sport doesn't exist the way it does without the women who opened the door first. Sparky D was there before there was a lane. No pitch, no product in this one — just respect. Rest easy to a pioneer.\n\n## Sources\n- Complex — MC Sparky D, Roxanne Wars icon, dies: https://www.complex.com/music/a/markelibert/mc-sparky-d-roxanne-wars-icon-dies\n- theGrio — Sparky D dies at 61: https://thegrio.com/2026/07/08/mc-sparky-d-death-roxanne-wars-icon-dies-61/\n- Wikipedia — Sparky D: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sparky_D\n\nBuilt for the culture. Operated from San Diego. Run by PHRHX through Sneakz & Beatz LLC. Black-owned, four pillars: sneakers, hip-hop, anime, gaming.",
