    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.pushsquare.com/news/2026/07/the-elder-scrolls-6-is-reportedly-still-years-away-from-release",
    "body": "The most-wanted open-world RPG on the planet is also one of the least-seen. The Elder Scrolls VI got a teaser in 2018 and has been mostly silence since — and the latest reporting says the wait isn't close to over.\n\n## Two to three years, at least\nIn a recent industry Q&A, journalist Jason Schreier said the game is still 'two to three years away at least.' That lines up with a project that's been in the background while Bethesda shipped other games first, and it puts any realistic launch deep into the back half of the decade.\n\n## The layoffs are the new hook\nAs part of Xbox's mass layoffs in July 2026, reports pointed to more than 50 job losses at Bethesda Game Studios — cuts that reportedly shattered morale and could push development further out. A game this size doesn't get easier to finish when the team building it gets smaller.\n\n## Why this lane cares\nThe Elder Scrolls is the blueprint for the big-world, single-player RPG — the exact space this show favors. Skyrim is still being played and re-released more than a decade later. Its successor carries expectations almost no game could meet, and every year of delay raises them higher.\n\n## The honest read\nThis isn't a game slipping because it's broken — it's the reality of an enormous project inside a studio taking hits. Report it straight: the RPG everyone's waiting on just moved a little further down the road, and the reasons have as much to do with the business as the game.\n\n## Sources\n- Push Square — TES6 reportedly still years away: https://www.pushsquare.com/news/2026/07/the-elder-scrolls-6-is-reportedly-still-years-away-from-release\n- GamingBible — TES6 launch window, layoffs: https://www.gamingbible.com/news/platform/xbox/the-elder-scrolls-6-launch-window-lay-offs-149673-20260708\n- Wikipedia — The Elder Scrolls VI: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Elder_Scrolls_VI\n\nBuilt for the culture. Operated from San Diego. Run by PHRHX through Sneakz & Beatz LLC. Black-owned, four pillars: sneakers, hip-hop, anime, gaming.",
