    "body": "The first Edgerunners took a video-game tie-in and turned it into one of the most gut-punching anime of its year. The sequel just showed its hand — and it's not running the same story back.\n\n## The full crew, finally named\nEdgerunners 2 revealed its four leads: Weak Kingsley, a veteran edgerunner living in the shadow of his former glory; Roman Carax, a young cinephile obsessed with documenting other people's lives; Talia Yang, a corpo-raised woman who's embraced a life of chrome and violence; and D, a Snake Nation netrunner driven by revenge after his clan was wiped out.\n\n## A standalone story\nLike the first season, it's a self-contained arc — no prior viewing required — set in the same Night City. A new teaser landed on the official Cyberpunk channel confirming a Fall 2026 Netflix window. New faces, new crew, same machine that chews people up.\n\n## Why the reveal is the news\nWe ran the trailer beat earlier; this is the next step — an actual cast with actual backstories, which is when a sequel stops being a rumor and starts being a show. The character mix (a documentarian, a revenge-driven netrunner, a corpo defector) tells you the tone before a single episode airs.\n\n## The crossover angle\nEdgerunners always mattered to us because it sits where anime meets the game meets the music — the first season lived on its soundtrack. A new crew in Night City keeps the biggest anime-gaming crossover of the decade in the feed, and we'll be watching what it sounds like as much as what it looks like.\n\n## Sources\n- Fiction Horizon — Edgerunners 2 reveals full crew, Fall 2026: https://fictionhorizon.com/cyberpunk-edgerunners-2-reveals-its-full-new-crew-and-a-fall-2026-release-window-that-has-night-city-fans-ready/\n- Crunchyroll News — Edgerunners season 2 Fall 2026 visual: https://www.crunchyroll.com/news/latest/2026/6/28/cyberpunk-edgerunners-season-2-fall-2026-release-date-visual\n- GamesRadar — Edgerunners season 2 everything we know: https://www.gamesradar.com/entertainment/anime-shows/cyberpunk-edgerunners-season-2-release-date-trailer-story/\n\nBuilt for the culture. Operated from San Diego. Run by PHRHX through Sneakz & Beatz LLC. Black-owned, four pillars: sneakers, hip-hop, anime, gaming.",
