    "ogHeadline": "No. 2 debut.\n16 of 18 charted.",
    "ogAccent": "7A3FF2",
    "heroCredit": "Billboard",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.billboard.com/",
    "body": "Forget the tour drama for one second and just read the board. 'Bully,' Ye's twelfth studio album, opened at No. 2 on the Billboard 200 with roughly 152,000 equivalent album units in its first week. That's a real number in 2026, when the whole industry runs on streams and attention moves in an afternoon.\n\nThe stat that jumps out sits on the singles chart. Sixteen of the album's eighteen tracks landed on the Hot 100 at the same time. You don't get that from one hit and a lot of filler. You get that when people press play at track one and let the thing run — front to back, on repeat, enough of them to move the needle across almost the whole tracklist.\n\n## What the number actually means\n\nCharting sixteen songs in a single week is rare air. It says the audience treated 'Bully' like an album, not a playlist to cherry-pick. For an artist this deep into a catalog, that kind of top-to-bottom engagement is the harder thing to pull off than a lead single. New acts get a viral moment. Veterans get their whole body of work streamed on faith. This is the second kind.\n\n## The split-screen\n\nNone of this happens in a vacuum. The tour behind the album ran into cancellations across Europe, and the conversation around Ye has been loud for years. We report that straight, same as we report the chart. Both things are true at once: the live run took hits abroad, and the record still performed like a headliner at home. You can hold both without spinning either.\n\nFor a beatmaker, the takeaway is craft-level. Cohesion sells. An album that people run end-to-end beats a collection of loosies fighting for the same slot. That's the lesson under the number, whatever you think of the man who put it up.\n\n## Sources\n- Wikipedia — Ye Live Concert Tour (album chart figures, tour cancellations): https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ye_Live_Concert_Tour\n- Billboard — Kanye West summer tour adds Chicago, San Antonio shows: https://www.billboard.com/music/rb-hip-hop/kanye-west-summer-tour-adds-chicago-san-antonio-shows-1236272815/\n\nBuilt for the culture. Operated from San Diego. Run by PHRHX through Sneakz & Beatz LLC. Black-owned, four pillars: sneakers, hip-hop, anime, gaming.",
