    "heroCredit": "Polyarc",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.polyarcgames.com/games/moss",
    "body": "The big single-player names are all on the horizon. Moss: The Forgotten Relic is here now — or close enough. Polyarc's adventure drops July 16 on PS5, Xbox, Switch and PC, and the headline for a lot of players is simple: no headset required this time.\n\nThe Moss series started in VR, built around Quill, the little mouse hero you guided through a storybook world. Bringing it to a flat screen opens it up to everybody who liked the look but never strapped on goggles. Same story-driven, hand-crafted feel; a lot more people who can actually play it.\n\n## Small, but it counts\n\nLet's keep it honest — this isn't a GTA or an Elder Scrolls. It's a tighter, cozier adventure, and that's the point. It's also one of the few brand-new single-player titles actually shipping this week while the giants stay parked on the calendar. For a lane built on solo, story-first games, a real release beats another trailer for something two years out.\n\n## Who it's for\n\nIf you want something you can start and finish, with a clear story and a world made by hand instead of generated, this is a clean pickup. Play it on the couch, no setup, no motion sickness, just the adventure. Sometimes the palette cleanser between blockbusters is exactly what the lane needs.\n\n## Sources\n- Gematsu — Moss: The Forgotten Relic launches July 16: https://www.gematsu.com/2026/06/moss-the-forgotten-relic-launches-july-16\n- PlayStation Store — Moss: The Forgotten Relic: https://store.playstation.com/en-us/concept/10017247/\n- Polyarc — Moss games: https://www.polyarcgames.com/games/moss\n\nBuilt for the culture. Operated from San Diego. Run by PHRHX through Sneakz & Beatz LLC. Black-owned, four pillars: sneakers, hip-hop, anime, gaming.",
