    "ogHeadline": "Loud, clean,\nand a 4.",
    "ogAccent": "C0392B",
    "heroCredit": "Sneaker Bar Detroit",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://sneakerbardetroit.com/",
    "body": "The Air Jordan 4 'Comic' drops July 25 at $220, and it's the first big retro up in a stacked late-summer run. White upper, fire-pink and light arctic-pink accents, muslin base — a bright, print-inspired take on the silhouette that basically prints money.\n\nThe 4 doesn't need a gimmick to sell. It's one of the most bankable shapes in the whole Jordan line. So when they put a loud summer colorway on it, the question isn't whether it moves — it's whether you like it enough to chase it.\n\n## Why the 4 stays untouchable\n\nThe 4 is the everyman grail. It's got the visible support, the mesh panels, the shape that reads clean with jeans or shorts. That's why it carries loud colorways better than most models — the silhouette is strong enough to hold color without tipping into costume. 'Comic' leans on that.\n\n## The colorway read\n\nThe fire-pink and arctic-pink combo on a muslin base is a warm-weather play. It's a summer shoe, plain and simple — bright enough to catch eyes, clean enough that you'll still wear it in the fall. The 'Comic' name and the print-inspired hits give it a story without leaning on a full theme.\n\n## Where it sits on the calendar\n\nJuly 25 puts it right before an August loaded with retros. Leading a run like this matters — the first strong pair sets the tone and takes early attention before the calendar gets crowded. At $220 it's priced like a standard premium 4, not a grail markup.\n\nIf you buy one Jordan this month for actual rotation, a bright 4 is the safe, correct pick. It's the shoe you wear, not the one you sit in a box.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Air Jordan retro 2026 release dates (Sneaker Bar Detroit)](https://sneakerbardetroit.com/air-jordan-retro-spring-2026-release-dates/)\n- [Air Jordan release dates (Nice Kicks)](https://www.nicekicks.com/air-jordan-release-dates/)",
