    "ogHeadline": "Navy, flint,\ndone.",
    "ogAccent": "C0392B",
    "heroCredit": "Nice Kicks",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.nicekicks.com/",
    "body": "The Air Jordan 13 'Flint' is back August 1 at $215. Navy, flint grey, university blue — the OG colorway that's been quietly in people's rotations since the '90s. No gimmick, no theme. Just a clean shoe.\n\nThe 13 is a sleeper. It doesn't get the noise the 1, 3, or 4 pull, but the people who wear their shoes know it's one of the most comfortable, most wearable models Jordan ever put out. 'Flint' is the colorway that makes the case.\n\n## The panther-paw shoe\n\nThe 13's sole was inspired by a panther's paw, and the hologram on the ankle is the detail that dates it perfectly to its era. On a loud colorway those details can read busy. On 'Flint' — navy with grey and a pop of blue — they read like a suit. Grown and clean.\n\n## Why 'Flint' specifically\n\nThis is an OG colorway, not a made-up remix. That matters to the people who care about the 13's history. It's the pair that ties to Jordan's late Bulls run, and the navy tone makes it one of the easiest Jordans to actually build outfits around. You're not matching a costume — you're matching a neutral.\n\n## Same day, tough choice\n\n'Flint' shares August 1 with the Air Jordan 1 High OG 'Love The Game.' If your budget's picking one, it comes down to lane: the 1 is the culture's center of gravity, the 13 is the sleeper comfort play. Both are correct. Neither is a mistake.\n\nIf you want the shoe you'll reach for on a random Tuesday without thinking, 'Flint' is that shoe.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Air Jordan release dates 2026 (Nice Kicks)](https://www.nicekicks.com/air-jordan-release-dates/)\n- [Air Jordan 2026 & 2027 calendar (JustFreshKicks)](https://justfreshkicks.com/air-jordan-release-dates/)",
