    "ogHeadline": "Meet your hero.\nNow the problem.",
    "ogAccent": "00E0C6",
    "heroCredit": "GamesRadar",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.gamesradar.com/",
    "body": "The Fable reboot came back with a new Xbox Showcase trailer, and it pulled a real move. It builds the whole thing around Isabel, the Hero of Wraithmarsh, voiced by Hayley Atwell — and then flips it, revealing she's a central antagonist of the adventure. More short film than gameplay reel, and people ate it up.\n\nThat's a smart way to reintroduce a series that's been gone a long time. Instead of another 'here's our world' montage, they gave you a character to attach to, then complicated her. It sticks.\n\n## The antagonist twist\n\nMaking your framing character the villain is a storytelling flex. It tells you Fable's leaning back into the moral-choice DNA the series was built on — a world where hero and villain aren't clean categories. Atwell's casting gives it weight; she can carry both the charm and the menace the twist needs.\n\n## Trailer, not launch\n\nBe clear-eyed: Fable's a 2027 game. This is a look, not a release. Playground Games — the Forza Horizon studio — is building it, and a cinematic trailer this far out is about keeping the game in the conversation, not selling you a date. That's fine. It worked.\n\n## Why it lands in this lane\n\nThis show runs on big-world, single-player RPGs, and Fable is exactly that — a story-driven adventure in a hand-built world with real choices. A trailer that gets people theorizing about a hero-turned-villain is the kind of thing that keeps an RPG alive for months between showings. That's the game staying warm.\n\nWe'll see the actual game when they're ready. For now, they gave us a hero worth caring about and a reason not to trust her. Good hook.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [New RPG trailers June 2026 incl. Fable (GamesRadar)](https://www.gamesradar.com/new-rpgs-trailers-june-2026/)\n- [Fable (2027 video game) (Wikipedia)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fable_(2027_video_game))",
