    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.whats-on-netflix.com/",
    "body": "Jujutsu Kaisen Season 3 — 'The Culling Game Part 1' — hits Netflix worldwide on July 22. That's a global same-day drop, no staggered regional windows, for the arc that turns the whole sorcerer world into a live battle royale. The TV run wrapped in late March; now the streaming wave hits everybody at once.\n\nIf you fell off after the last season or you're jumping back in, this is the clean entry point. Same day, everywhere, one place to watch.\n\n## What the Culling Game is\n\nAfter Shibuya blew the story open, Kenjaku sets loose the Culling Game — a deadly contest that drags sorcerers and the newly awakened into a fight for survival across sealed-off zones. It's the arc that raises the stakes and reshuffles who matters. Part 1 covers the opening half of it.\n\n## Why the global drop is the story\n\nA worldwide same-day release is Netflix treating this like a tentpole, not a niche anime. It means the conversation happens everywhere simultaneously — no waiting weeks for your region, no dodging spoilers from overseas. For a series this big on social, that synchronized drop is going to light up timelines the day it lands.\n\n## The bar it's walking into\n\nSeason 2's Shibuya run trended every single week it aired. That's the expectation Season 3 walks into. The animation studio's been under a microscope, and a battle-royale arc is exactly the kind of material that either delivers spectacle or gets picked apart. Either way, people will be watching frame by frame.\n\nThis is appointment viewing. Clear the 22nd, dodge the spoilers, and watch the sorcerer world get a lot smaller.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [JJK S3 'The Culling Game' Netflix release date (What's on Netflix)](https://www.whats-on-netflix.com/news/anime/jujutsu-kaisen-the-culling-game-netflix-release-date/)\n- [Jujutsu Kaisen season 3 (GamesRadar)](https://www.gamesradar.com/jujutsu-kaisen-season-3-release-date-trailer-story-news-culling-games/)",
