    "ogAccent": "FF3E7F",
    "heroCredit": "Primetime Anime",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://primetimeanime.com/",
    "body": "One Piece is finally animating Elbaf. The land of giants — teased since the earliest stretches of the story, name-dropped for two decades — is moving on screen as a marquee stop in the final saga. For long-time fans, this is one of those payoffs you half-doubted you'd ever actually see.\n\nThat's the weight here. Elbaf isn't a random island of the week. It's been sitting in the lore as a promise, and the anime reaching it is a milestone, not a filler stop.\n\n## Twenty years of setup\n\nGo back to the early arcs and the giants were already part of the mythology — warriors, honor, a homeland the story kept pointing at. Elbaf pays that off. When a series builds a place up for this long, arriving there carries a payoff no new location can match. The anticipation is baked in.\n\n## Why it pulls people back\n\nOne Piece is deep into its run, and a marquee final-saga arc is exactly what brings lapsed fans back to the couch. 'Wait till Elbaf' has been a fandom line for years. Now the answer's on screen. That's the kind of moment that turns a casual check-in into a full rewatch spiral.\n\n## The final-saga stakes\n\nThis late in the story, every major arc moves the endgame. Elbaf isn't a side quest — the giants and their homeland tie into the bigger threads the series is racing toward. The anime putting it in motion means the payoffs are getting closer, not further.\n\nTwo-plus decades of buildup, and the Straw Hats finally made it to the giants. If you've been riding since the early days, this is your reward.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [New anime release dates 2026 schedule (Primetime Anime)](https://primetimeanime.com/blog/new-anime-release-dates-2026-complete-schedule)\n- [Most anticipated anime of summer 2026 (Screen Rant)](https://screenrant.com/most-anticipated-summer-2026-anime/)",
