    "ogAccent": "FF3E7F",
    "heroCredit": "Screen Rant",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://screenrant.com/",
    "body": "Dorohedoro Season 2 is coming, and MAPPA — the Chainsaw Man studio — has it. The show picks Caiman's story back up: a man with a lizard's head and no memory, tearing through the Hole to hunt the sorcerers who did this to him. Violent, funny, gross, and structurally strange in the best way.\n\nSeason 1 built a hard cult following and then the show went quiet for years. Fans have been waiting. A confirmed second season at a top studio is the payoff.\n\n## What makes it a cult favorite\n\nDorohedoro doesn't look or move like anything else. It's set in a grimy dual-world of the Hole and the Sorcerers' realm, it swings between brutal violence and genuine comedy in the same scene, and it's built around a mystery — who was Caiman before the lizard head. That mix is why the people who love it really love it.\n\n## Why MAPPA matters here\n\nStudio makes the difference on material this weird. MAPPA's got the range to handle the ugliness and the humor without flattening either. A cult source plus a top-tier studio is the exact setup that turns a quiet favorite into appointment TV — the same way strong adaptations have elevated other dark manga.\n\n## The long wait pays off\n\nSeason 1 ended on threads fans have chewed on for years. Season 2 continuing the hunt — Caiman, En's crew of sorcerers, the mystery under it all — is what the cult's been asking for. For the heads who like their anime mean and unusual, this is a return worth marking.\n\nThe lizard-head's back, and the studio behind him is stacked. That's the setup.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Most anticipated anime of summer 2026 (Screen Rant)](https://screenrant.com/most-anticipated-summer-2026-anime/)\n- [New anime release dates 2026 schedule (Primetime Anime)](https://primetimeanime.com/blog/new-anime-release-dates-2026-complete-schedule)",
