    "heroCreditUrl": "https://versetracker.com/events/url-ultimate-rap-league-summer-madness-15",
    "body": "Off the timeline: URL loaded up Summer Madness 15, and the name that jumped out is Loaded Lux. Lux vs Twork is on the card, and for anybody who's watched this sport for real, a Lux booking on the biggest stage is an event by itself.\n\nSummer Madness is URL's flagship — the Super Bowl of the culture. Putting a legend on it isn't filler, it's a headline.\n\n## Why Lux still moves the room\n\nLoaded Lux is one of the most studied pens in battle rap history. When he steps on stage the whole sport pays attention, because his rounds get broken down line by line for months. He doesn't battle often, so every appearance carries weight. That scarcity is the point.\n\n## The rest of the card\n\nHe's not the only draw. Summer Madness 15 also lines up Geechi Gotti vs Shotty Horroh — Gotti being one of the most consistent performers of this era. A card that pairs a technician-legend with active-era headliners is exactly why people still buy the pay-per-view.\n\n## Where we stand on it\n\nOur lane is showing love to hip-hop in the places the mainstream skips, and battle rap is at the top of that list. Black battlers, on the sport's biggest platform, in a room that rewards actual writing. Lux back on a Summer Madness card is the kind of thing that reminds you this culture has its own legends and its own history.\n\nMark it. When the footage drops, it's getting clipped everywhere.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Summer Madness 15 — URL (VerseTracker)](https://versetracker.com/events/url-ultimate-rap-league-summer-madness-15)\n- [Ultimate Rap League (@urltv) on X](https://x.com/urltv)",
