    "body": "The one the culture's actually reacting to this month: the Air Jordan 8 'BIN 23.' It's Jordan Brand's ultra-premium play — reportedly limited to 2,300 individually numbered pairs, dropping August 15 at $355. That's not a general release, that's a grail setup.\n\nThe 8 is a sleeper silhouette. Give it a luxury treatment and a hard number cap, and it turns into a chase.\n\n## What 'numbered' does to a shoe\n\nIndividually numbered pairs change the whole conversation. Every box is one of a known, small total — 2,300 in this case. That scarcity is the product. It's why the resale talk starts the second a shoe like this leaks, and why the people who get one treat it different.\n\n## $355 and worth watching\n\nAt $355 this isn't the everyman 8. It's the top-shelf version, and it's priced to say so. Whether you cop or just watch, it's the sneaker headline of the mid-August calendar — the one that pulls attention away from the standard retros sharing the month.\n\n## Where it sits on the board\n\nAugust is stacked with Jordan retros, but most are general releases. The BIN 23 is the exception — the limited, numbered, premium anchor that the whole month gets measured against. Lead the sneaker talk with it because it's the one moving the timeline.\n\nLoud in a quiet way: no wild colorway, just a number on the box and a cap on how many exist.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Every Air Jordan releasing in August 2026 (Men's Journal)](https://www.mensjournal.com/style/air-jordan-release-date-calendar-august-of-2026)\n- [Air Jordan release dates 2026 (Sneaker Bar Detroit)](https://sneakerbardetroit.com/air-jordan-release-dates/)",
