    "body": "Cyberpunk always gets a beat, and this one's a game story so it lives in gaming. CD Projekt Red announced Update 2.4, the 'Afterlife Edition' — being marketed as the last numbered content drop for Cyberpunk 2077. The catch everybody's laughing about: they already said the last one was the last one.\n\nFive-plus years after a disaster launch, the game is finally the thing they promised in 2018. This update is the send-off.\n\n## What's actually in it\n\nThe 2.4 drop reportedly bundles a surprise Edgerunners 2 anime tie-in patch, a fresh wave of community mods built on the rebuilt REDmod toolchain, and a free Trauma Team cosmetic set to mark the milestone. It's shipping in three waves instead of one big drop — partly to spread server load, partly to give modders room to update between waves.\n\n## Why it hits for the single-player crowd\n\nThis is a single-player RPG that got rebuilt in public. The people who stuck around through the patch-by-patch redemption arc are exactly who this is for. Closing out V's story with a content drop that respects them — instead of just walking away — is the right way to end an era.\n\n## The bigger move\n\nAfter 2.4, CDPR pivots fully to Project Orion, the sequel, with a reveal rumored for 2027 or 2028. So this update is a line in the sand: the V era gets its ending, and the next Night City starts cooking. For a game this beloved in the RPG lane, that's a story worth the whole segment.\n\nThe game that wouldn't die gets one more, real ending.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [CD Projekt announces another surprise Cyberpunk 2077 update (PC Gamer)](https://www.pcgamer.com/games/rpg/the-last-one-wasnt-the-last-one-cd-projekt-has-cyber-punked-us-again-announcing-another-surprise-update-for-cyberpunk-2077/)\n- [Cyberpunk 2077 is getting another final 'final' update (Game8)](https://game8.co/articles/latest/cyberpunk-2077-is-getting-another-final-final-update)",
