    "body": "Anime lead, and it's the biggest one there is: Demon Slayer: Infinity Castle is coming to streaming. Crunchyroll is putting the film up on July 28, a date confirmed around its Anime Expo panel. The movie that ran up over $780 million in theaters finally hits home screens.\n\nIf you missed it in a theater, this is the moment. If you saw it twice, you already know why this is appointment viewing.\n\n## A record-breaker, not just a hit\n\nInfinity Castle didn't just do well — it rewrote records, pulling in north of $780M worldwide and landing near-perfect audience scores. It's the biggest anime feature of its era, the first chapter of the trilogy that closes out the series. A film that size moving to streaming is a cultural event, not a quiet catalog add.\n\n## Why the streaming date is the story\n\nThe theatrical run already had its moment. The news now is access — a global streaming drop means the whole fanbase, including everyone who couldn't catch it in a theater, gets it at once. That's what turns a July date into a trending week.\n\n## What it sets up\n\nThis is chapter one of a trilogy. Getting the first film in front of the widest possible audience right now keeps the momentum rolling toward the next two. For the 25-45 anime crowd that grew up on this run, it's a full-circle moment finally landing where everybody can hit play.\n\nBiggest anime film of the era, one click away. That's the headline.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Infinity Castle streaming date after $794M box office (Forbes)](https://www.forbes.com/sites/timlammers/2026/07/04/demon-slayer-infinity-castle-streaming-date-nears-after-film-earns-794-million-in-theaters/)\n- [Demon Slayer: Infinity Castle (Wikipedia)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Demon_Slayer:_Kimetsu_no_Yaiba_%E2%80%93_The_Movie:_Infinity_Castle)",
