    "heroCredit": "Anireload",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://anireload.com/list-of-upcoming-anime-in-july-2026/",
    "body": "Not every anime story is a shonen giant. Sparks of Tomorrow — a Kyoto Animation original adapting Hiro Yuki's light novel — landed on Netflix July 5, and the reason it matters is the name on the door: KyoAni.\n\nFor a certain kind of fan, a new Kyoto Animation project is bigger than any single IP.\n\n## Why KyoAni carries weight\n\nKyoto Animation is the studio behind some of the most visually gorgeous, emotionally precise anime ever made — the kind of craft that made them a fan-favorite for a generation. After everything the studio has been through, every new project is watched with more care and more rooting interest than a normal release gets.\n\n## What Sparks of Tomorrow is\n\nIt's a light-novel adaptation getting the full KyoAni treatment on a global platform. Netflix distribution means it drops worldwide at once, no import barrier. For a studio original, that reach is a big deal — it puts the animation in front of the widest possible room.\n\n## The comeback angle\n\nThis isn't about chart-topping numbers. It's about a beloved studio steadily getting back to doing what it does best, and a new project landing where anyone can watch it. For the 25-45 crowd that came up on KyoAni's classics, that's a quietly meaningful drop.\n\nBig names aren't only the loud ones. Sometimes it's a studio you're just glad to see back.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Upcoming anime in July 2026 (Anireload)](https://anireload.com/list-of-upcoming-anime-in-july-2026/)\n- [New anime release guide July 2026 (Complex)](https://www.complex.com/pop-culture/a/khal/anime-release-guide)",
