    "heroCreditUrl": "https://screenrant.com/cyberpunk-2077-july-2026-sales-update/",
    "body": "Cyberpunk always gets a beat on this show, and this episode it's a game story, so it sits in gaming. The number: as of early July, Cyberpunk 2077 has sold 40 million copies worldwide.\n\nSit with that. This is the game that launched in 2020 so broken it got pulled from a storefront.\n\n## The redemption arc, in one stat\n\nForty million is not a quiet recovery — it's one of the best-selling games of its generation. The 2.0 overhaul and the Phantom Liberty expansion turned the reputation around, and word of mouth did the rest. A launch that became a punchline is now a case study in patching your way back to greatness.\n\n## Why CDPR keeps feeding it\n\nThe sales are exactly why CD Projekt keeps shipping surprise updates and spin-offs instead of walking away. There's a living audience in Night City, and the studio keeps giving them reasons to stay while the Orion sequel cooks in the background. A game that 'wouldn't die' is a game people won't stop buying.\n\n## The lane read\n\nWe track gaming by real engagement, and few single-player games hold a community like this one has. Forty million copies is proof the story-first, big-world lane still wins when the work gets done. The comeback isn't a narrative anymore — it's a receipt.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Cyberpunk 2077 July 2026 sales update (ScreenRant)](https://screenrant.com/cyberpunk-2077-july-2026-sales-update/)\n- [Cyberpunk 2077 official news (CD Projekt Red)](https://www.cyberpunk.net/en/news/)",
