    "ogHeadline": "25 years.\nStill Spira.",
    "ogAccent": "3B6FB0",
    "heroCredit": "Siliconera",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.siliconera.com/switch-2-final-fantasy-x-x-2-hd-remaster-arrives-for-25th-anniversary/",
    "body": "Host lane means single-player RPGs, and few carry the weight of this one. Final Fantasy X turns 25, and Square Enix is marking it by bringing the FFX/X-2 HD Remaster to Nintendo Switch 2 — digital on July 23, with a physical edition following August 27.\n\nFFX first hit PS2 in 2001. A quarter century later, it's still the game a lot of people name when they name the best RPG ever made.\n\n## Why FFX still holds up\n\nThis is the entry that pushed the series into full voice acting and cinematic storytelling. The Sphere Grid, the turn-based combat, and a story about Tidus and Yuna that people still get emotional about — it landed at exactly the right moment and never really faded. A remaster on new hardware just makes it easy to hand to a new player.\n\n## The Switch 2 fit\n\nPutting a 60-plus-hour single-player RPG on a portable is the whole pitch. FFX is built for long, focused runs, and being able to play it handheld or docked is how a lot of people prefer to sink into a game like this. The anniversary timing — FFX hit 25 on July 19 — makes it a moment, not just a re-release.\n\n## Where it lands for us\n\nIn a July stacked with remakes, a proper JRPG landmark coming to the newest Nintendo box is a clean host-lane pick. Story-first, big world, single-player through and through. If you never played it, this is your on-ramp.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Switch 2 Final Fantasy X/X-2 HD Remaster arrives for 25th anniversary (Siliconera)](https://www.siliconera.com/switch-2-final-fantasy-x-x-2-hd-remaster-arrives-for-25th-anniversary/)\n- [FFX/X-2 HD Remaster coming to Switch 2 on 23 July 2026 (The Otaku's Study)](https://www.otakustudy.com/video-game/2026/06/final-fantasy-x-x-2-hd-remaster-coming-to-nintendo-switch-2-on-23-july-2026/)",
