    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.animationmagazine.net/2026/07/science-sarus-new-the-ghost-in-the-shell-series-premieres-on-prime-video-on-july-7/",
    "body": "Anime lead, and it's a legend coming back. The new Ghost in the Shell — a full reboot from Science SARU — premiered worldwide on Prime Video on July 7, and it's already climbing the charts.\n\nFor anybody who cares about cyberpunk, this is the source. The 1995 film shaped a whole aesthetic. A fresh take is a big deal.\n\n## The studio behind it\n\nScience SARU is the house behind Dandadan and Ping Pong the Animation — a studio with a real visual identity, not a factory. Director Mokochan makes their anime debut here, with the pedigree of a team known for taking swings. That's the right kind of energy for a property this iconic.\n\n## What it's actually about\n\nThe series is set in 2029 and follows Major Motoko Kusanagi — a full-body cyborg — and the Public Security Section 9 team as they hunt the AI known as the Puppet Master. It's the core Ghost in the Shell premise: identity, consciousness, and what's left of 'you' when the body is machine. Ten episodes, dropping weekly instead of all at once.\n\n## Why it's connecting\n\nIt defied the odds to become one of Prime Video's most popular series out the gate — early word on the first episode has been strong. A weekly release keeps the conversation alive, which is exactly how a slow-burn cyberpunk story should roll out. The classic still has pull.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Science SARU's Ghost in the Shell premieres on Prime Video July 7 (Animation Magazine)](https://www.animationmagazine.net/2026/07/science-sarus-new-the-ghost-in-the-shell-series-premieres-on-prime-video-on-july-7/)\n- [The Ghost in the Shell release schedule (GamesRadar)](https://www.gamesradar.com/entertainment/anime-shows/the-ghost-in-the-shell-release-date-time-schedule-prime-video/)",
