    "pillar": "gaming",
    "title": "GTA 6 Trailer Watch: The Ramp Before November",
    "headline": "November's Locked.\nThe Wait Is Loud.",
    "subhead": "GTA 6 is still dated for November 19, and this weekend the internet has itself convinced Trailer 3 rides the July 19 World Cup final. Here's the confirmed part — and the part that's just hope.",
    "description": "GTA 6 is confirmed for November 19, 2026 (preload Nov 12), and fans expect a third trailer around the July 19 World Cup final. What Rockstar has actually said vs. what the community is speculating.",
    "keywords": [
      "GTA 6 trailer 3",
      "GTA 6 release date",
      "Grand Theft Auto VI 2026",
      "GTA 6 November 19",
      "Rockstar Games",
      "GTA 6 gameplay trailer",
      "Sneakz and Beatz",
      "PHRHX"
    ],
    "ogHeadline": "November's locked.\nThe wait is loud.",
    "ogAccent": "6A1B9A",
    "heroCredit": "GamesRadar+",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.gamesradar.com/gta-6-guide/",
    "body": "No game moves the internet like this one. So let's separate what Rockstar has actually confirmed from what the timeline wants to be true.\n\n## What's confirmed\nGrand Theft Auto VI is scheduled for November 19, 2026 on PlayStation 5 and Xbox Series X|S, with a digital preload set for November 12. Two trailers exist so far — the first in December 2023, the second in May 2025. That's the solid ground.\n\n## What's speculation (flagged)\nHere's the rumor part, and we're calling it a rumor: fans are convinced a third trailer is landing this weekend, riding the July 19 World Cup final — the exact kind of social-first global stage Rockstar has said it wants. Some point at that date, others at an early-August earnings window, with a separate gameplay trailer to follow. Rockstar has not confirmed any of it. It's a community reading the tea leaves of a summer marketing window — not an announcement.\n\n## Why it's the gaming lead anyway\nBecause nothing else in gaming pulls these numbers. Every GTA 6 video, leak, and countdown racks up millions of views on name alone, and this is a single-player, open-world monster — dead center of the lane the show lives in. When the biggest game on earth is one trailer away from breaking the day it drops, that's the story, even before the trailer exists.\n\n## What to actually watch\nIgnore the fan-made countdowns. Watch Rockstar's own channels and Newswire. When they move, the whole calendar moves with them.\n\nNovember is real. The trailer is a maybe. Keep your expectations where the facts are — and your notifications on.\n\n## Sources\n- GamesRadar+ — GTA 6: everything we know: https://www.gamesradar.com/gta-6-guide/\n- Wikipedia — Grand Theft Auto VI: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grand_Theft_Auto_VI\n- GamingBible — fans convinced they know the date of GTA 6's next reveal: https://www.gamingbible.com/news/gta-6-trailer-reveal-august-7-865500-20260710\n",
