    "slug": "echoes-of-aincrad-sao-2026",
    "pillar": "gaming",
    "title": "Echoes of Aincrad Brings SAO Back to the Floor",
    "headline": "Cleared to\nFloor One.",
    "subhead": "Echoes of Aincrad, the Sword Art Online souls-like, is out now — a single-player run through the arc that started it all.",
    "description": "Echoes of Aincrad, a Sword Art Online souls-like action RPG, released July 10, 2026. A single-player run through the original Aincrad arc that started it all.",
    "keywords": [
      "Echoes of Aincrad",
      "Sword Art Online game 2026",
      "SAO souls-like",
      "single player RPG July 2026",
      "Aincrad arc game",
      "Sneakz and Beatz",
      "PHRHX",
      "single player RPG"
    ],
    "ogHeadline": "Cleared to\nfloor one.",
    "ogAccent": "1565C0",
    "heroCredit": "GameSpot",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.gamespot.com/articles/the-biggest-new-game-releases-of-july-2026/",
    "body": "Sword Art Online has had a rough history in games — a lot of tie-ins, not a lot of keepers. This one's swinging bigger.\n\n## What it is\nEchoes of Aincrad is a Sword Art Online action RPG built with a souls-like structure, released July 10, 2026. It runs through the first Aincrad arc of the original light novels — the death-game floors that made SAO a phenomenon in the first place.\n\n## Why the format fits\nA souls-like is the right shape for Aincrad. The whole premise is a tower you clear floor by floor, where a mistake actually costs you. Building the combat around weight, risk, and earned progress lines up with the source material better than the arena tie-ins ever did.\n\n## Why it's on the show\nIt's single-player, it's a world you get lost in, and it's got an anime hook — right in the lane we ride for. It's also the kind of mid-size RPG that overperforms when the combat's good and the fanbase is starving for a real one.\n\n## The honest caveat\nSouls-likes live and die on feel. If the swing weight and boss design land, this is the SAO game people have been asking for. If they don't, it's another tie-in. Early on either way, it's worth a look for anyone who wants a story-driven run this month.\n\nThe floors are open. Time to see if this one clears.\n\n## Sources\n- GameSpot — the biggest new game releases of July 2026: https://www.gamespot.com/articles/the-biggest-new-game-releases-of-july-2026/\n- RPG Site — the RPGs of 2026: every RPG and their release dates: https://www.rpgsite.net/feature/16349-the-rpgs-2026-every-rpg-their-release-dates\n",
    "publishedAt": "2026-07-17",
