    "pillar": "anime",
    "title": "Edgerunners 2 Reveals Its Crew and Its Window",
    "headline": "New Crew.\nFall Window.",
    "subhead": "Cyberpunk: Edgerunners 2 has shown off its full new cast and a Fall 2026 release window — the Night City fixture moves from teaser to real.",
    "description": "Cyberpunk: Edgerunners 2 revealed its full new crew and a Fall (Q4) 2026 release window — a standalone 10-episode sequel from Studio Trigger and CD Projekt Red.",
    "keywords": [
      "Cyberpunk Edgerunners 2",
      "Edgerunners season 2 release window",
      "Edgerunners 2 crew",
      "Cyberpunk 2077 anime",
      "Studio Trigger CDPR",
      "Sneakz and Beatz",
      "PHRHX",
      "anime 2026"
    ],
    "ogHeadline": "New crew.\nFall window.",
    "ogAccent": "E91E63",
    "heroCredit": "ScreenRant",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://screenrant.com/cyberpunk-2077-prequel-edgerunners-teasers-july-2026/",
    "body": "We caught the first look already. This is the follow-up that matters: a full crew and an actual window.\n\n## What's new\nCyberpunk: Edgerunners 2 has now revealed its complete new cast and locked a Fall 2026 release window — a Q4 landing, somewhere in the September-to-November stretch. That's the step past a teaser: names, faces, and a season to circle.\n\n## The shape of it\nIt's a standalone 10-episode sequel from Studio Trigger and CD Projekt Red, set after the first season with a brand-new story and a fresh set of characters. Same Night City, different crew — the anthology approach that keeps the world alive without cheapening the original's complete, gut-punch arc.\n\n## Why it runs in anime\nHouse rule: Cyberpunk always gets a beat, placed by medium. This is anime news — a Trigger production — so it sits in the anime pillar, separate from anything happening on the game side.\n\n## Why it's a real moment\nThe first Edgerunners didn't just do numbers; it sent a wave of players straight back into Cyberpunk 2077 and rehabbed the whole brand. A second season with its own crew keeps that engine running while CD Projekt Red cooks the sequel. A new window means the flywheel spins again this fall.\n\nNight City's the star, and it's booked for the fall. The crew's new — the pull is the same.\n\n## Sources\n- ScreenRant — Cyberpunk 2077 prequel Edgerunners teasers July 2026: https://screenrant.com/cyberpunk-2077-prequel-edgerunners-teasers-july-2026/\n- Fiction Horizon — Edgerunners 2 reveals its full new crew and a Fall 2026 window: https://fictionhorizon.com/cyberpunk-edgerunners-2-reveals-its-full-new-crew-and-a-fall-2026-release-window-that-has-night-city-fans-ready/\n- Player.One — Edgerunners season 2 release window: https://www.player.one/cyberpunk-edgerunners-season-2-release-window-gives-cyberpunk-2077-fans-new-reason-return-163478\n",
