    "body": "Chainsaw Man is one of the biggest names MAPPA has. So when they open their mouth about what's next, the whole fandom leans in.\n\n## What was revealed\nAt its June 19, 2026 anniversary event, MAPPA put out new information on Chainsaw Man's upcoming sequel — the 'International Assassins Arc.' It's confirmation that the next major stretch of the story is officially in motion.\n\n## The catch (flagged)\nHere's the honest part. Reading MAPPA's past rollout timing, the anniversary reveal points to 2027 at the earliest for the actual return — Chainsaw Man is not slotted into any 2026 window. So this is a 'it's coming and here's the arc,' not a 'clear your calendar.' We're flagging that so nobody's refreshing Crunchyroll in the wrong year.\n\n## Why it still matters\nBecause the ceiling is enormous. The Reze arc film pushed the property to a new level, and the Assassins Arc is where the manga escalates hard. A confirmed direction from MAPPA is enough to keep this one near the top of every 'most anticipated' list — even with a patient timeline.\n\n## What to watch\nThe next real signal is a teaser or a dated trailer. Until MAPPA drops one, treat any specific date going around as a guess.\n\nThe contract's signed. The date's the only thing still up in the air.\n\n## Sources\n- GamesRadar+ — Chainsaw Man season 2 release date speculation and everything we know: https://www.gamesradar.com/chainsaw-man-season-2-release-date-cast-trailer-crunchyroll/\n- CBR — Jujutsu Kaisen, Attack on Titan and Chainsaw Man set for new reveals: https://www.cbr.com/jujutsu-kaisen-attack-on-titan-chainsaw-man-mappa-event/\n",
