    "ogHeadline": "Eleven years.\nOwn platform.",
    "ogAccent": "C0392B",
    "heroCredit": "Rap Grid — iBattleTV",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.rapgrid.com/leagues/ibattletv",
    "body": "Battle rap isn't just the two or three names that make the mainstream. The sport runs on independent rooms that built their own audience with no cosign. This week the beat goes to one of them: iBattleTV.\n\n## Who they are\niBattleTV is a battle rap platform with an archive spanning more than eleven years of events, commentary, and original series — a full catalog of cards streaming through its own PPV and subscription service. It's the kind of operation that built its own lane instead of waiting for a bigger league to open the door.\n\n## Why the clips travel\nThe value of a room like this is what happens after the night ends. Verses from iBattleTV cards get chopped, quoted, and reposted across X and YouTube, and that's where a lot of the audience actually meets the sport now. The event is the source; the timeline is the amplifier.\n\n## Why we're pointing here\nOur lane is showing love to hip-hop where the mainstream skips — battle rap, underground, independent Black-led platforms. iBattleTV is exactly that: a long-running room that gave battlers a stage and a paycheck outside the two biggest coastal leagues. We keep it at the platform level — respect for the operation, no invented card.\n\n## The bigger point\nEvery week we try to point new eyes at a different corner of the sport. The women had Queen of the Ring. The Midwest built Black Ice Cartel. iBattleTV is the archive that's been quietly stacking events for over a decade. Different rooms, same lesson: the culture stands on infrastructure that people built themselves.\n\nIf your battle rap knowledge stops at the biggest names, you're missing most of the map. Start digging.\n\n## Sources\n- Rap Grid — iBattleTV league page: https://www.rapgrid.com/leagues/ibattletv\n- VerseTracker — iBattleTV battles index: https://versetracker.com/battles/ibattletv\n- iBattleTV — official platform: https://ibattletv.vhx.tv/\n",
