    "pillar": "gaming",
    "title": "Beast of Reincarnation: Game Freak Goes Dark",
    "headline": "Pokémon's Studio.\nA Ruined Japan.",
    "subhead": "Beast of Reincarnation, Game Freak's dark action RPG, lands August 4 — the Pokémon studio's swing at a grown, single-player world.",
    "description": "Beast of Reincarnation, Game Freak's action RPG set in a ruined future Japan, releases August 4, 2026 on PC, PS5 and Xbox — around 30 hours across 10 stages.",
    "keywords": [
      "Beast of Reincarnation",
      "Game Freak RPG 2026",
      "Beast of Reincarnation release date",
      "single player RPG August 2026",
      "action RPG PS5",
      "Sneakz and Beatz",
      "PHRHX",
      "single player RPG"
    ],
    "ogHeadline": "Pokémon's studio.\na ruined Japan.",
    "ogAccent": "4A2C17",
    "heroCredit": "GameSpot",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.gamespot.com/articles/beast-of-reincarnation-release-date-trailer-news/1100-6539558/",
    "body": "Say Game Freak and most people think Pokémon. This is the studio betting it can do something completely different — dark, single-player, and grown.\n\n## What it is\nBeast of Reincarnation is an action RPG dropping players into a ruined, overgrown Japan roughly two thousand years in the future. It launches August 4, 2026 on PC, PS5 and Xbox Series X|S. After three decades of Pokémon, Game Freak is stepping into unfamiliar, moodier territory.\n\n## Not the souls-like you think\nIt looks souls-adjacent, but the director's been clear it isn't chasing that. Kota Furushima told Famitsu the goal is a game that's completable even for people who aren't action experts, with the option to lower difficulty. Parrying and a companion creature are in the mix — your dog actually helps you fight. It's built to welcome you, not wall you out.\n\n## The shape of it\nFurushima pegs it at around 30 hours across roughly 10 major stages. That's a focused, single-player run — not an open-world time sink — which is exactly the kind of story-driven size that overperforms when the combat and world click.\n\n## Why it's the gaming lead\nIt's single-player, it's a real world to get lost in, and it's a legacy studio taking a genuine creative swing. That's dead center of the lane the show rides for. The preview cycle's been loud for a reason: people want to see if Game Freak can build outside its comfort zone.\n\nThirty years of Pokémon, and now a dog, a sword, and a dead world. August 4 — this one's worth watching.\n\n## Sources\n- GameSpot — Beast of Reincarnation release date and everything we know: https://www.gamespot.com/articles/beast-of-reincarnation-release-date-trailer-news/1100-6539558/\n- Game Informer — Beast of Reincarnation preview, parrying helps your dog: https://gameinformer.com/preview/2026/07/13/parrying-helps-your-dog\n- Wikipedia — Beast of Reincarnation: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beast_of_Reincarnation\n",
