    "body": "Some games chase spectacle. A Plague Tale chases your gut. The series is back, and it's still one of the best single-player stories nobody talks about enough.\n\n## What's dropping\nResonance: A Plague Tale Legacy releases August 27, 2026 on PS5, Xbox Series X|S and PC. It's the next entry in Asobo's plague-era saga — the one built on story, atmosphere, and those unforgettable seas of rats.\n\n## Why the series lands\nInnocence and Requiem earned their following the hard way: tight, linear, brutally human stories where the horror is personal, not just monstrous. It's not an open world and it doesn't pretend to be. It's a crafted, single-player experience that trusts you to sit with heavy moments. That's a lane the show respects — story-first games made with real care.\n\n## What to watch for\nThe question with any Plague Tale follow-up is whether the tech and the tension keep pace with the writing. When the rat swarms hit their peak and the emotional beats land, this series does things almost nothing else does. If Resonance holds that bar, it's an easy August pick.\n\n## Where it fits\nBetween Beast of Reincarnation early in the month and the fall giants after it, late August is a smart window for a game that lives on story instead of noise. If you want a single-player run that actually stays with you, this is the one to clear time for.\n\nNot every big game is loud. Some of them just haunt you. August 27.\n\n## Sources\n- GameSpot — the biggest new game releases of July 2026: https://www.gamespot.com/articles/the-biggest-new-game-releases-of-july-2026/\n- VGC — upcoming video game release dates schedule: https://www.videogameschronicle.com/guide/upcoming-game-release-dates-schedule/\n- RPG Site — the RPGs of 2026: every RPG and their release dates: https://www.rpgsite.net/feature/16349-the-rpgs-2026-every-rpg-their-release-dates\n",
