    "slug": "url-ultimate-madness-tournament-2026",
    "pillar": "hiphop",
    "title": "URL Runs Its Own Madness Bracket",
    "headline": "Bracket Season.\nBig Stage.",
    "subhead": "The biggest Black-owned battle league in the world isn't waiting on anybody. URL announced a whole tournament — Ultimate Madness.",
    "description": "Smack/URL, the Black-owned Ultimate Rap League, announced a new bracket-style battle tournament called Ultimate Madness, keeping the culture on its own big stage.",
    "keywords": [
      "URL Ultimate Madness",
      "Ultimate Rap League",
      "Smack White",
      "Black-owned battle league",
      "battle rap 2026",
      "URLTV",
      "Sneakz and Beatz",
      "PHRHX"
    ],
    "ogHeadline": "Bracket season.\nBig stage.",
    "ogAccent": "8B1E1E",
    "heroCredit": "URLTV — Ultimate Rap League",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://urltv.tv/",
    "body": "Battle rap lives on the timeline, and this week the timeline points to the giant. URL announced a new tournament — Ultimate Madness — and it's a reminder of who's actually building the stages in this culture.\n\n## Who owns the room\nThe Ultimate Rap League — Smack/URL — is a New York battle league owned by Troy \"Smack White\" Mitchell, Eric Beasley and Jean \"Cheeko\" French out of Queens. It's the largest platform for MC battle culture on the planet, and it's Black-owned from the top. When we talk about showing love to hip-hop in more places than the mainstream, this is the blueprint: the people who built the art own the business.\n\n## What a tournament format changes\nA bracket flips the usual one-off battle into a run. Win and advance, lose and go home. That structure does something for the culture — it builds stakes across a season instead of a single night, and it forces the best to keep proving it. For battlers, a tournament is a shot at a title, not just a paycheck for one performance.\n\n## The Homecoming energy\nURL's been bringing big-stage battle rap back to New York with its Homecoming events — Smack putting the culture back on the biggest platform in its own backyard. Ultimate Madness rides that same wave: not renting someone else's spotlight, building the whole show in-house and letting the timeline do the marketing.\n\n## Why we lead with ownership\nEvery league we spotlight on the show, we lead with the same question — who signs the checks. URL answers it clean. The biggest name in battle rap is owned by the people who made it, and a new tournament is them betting on their own bracket. That's the story before a single matchup gets announced.\n\n## Sources\n- Ultimate Rap League (official) — https://urltv.tv/\n- AllHipHop: URL announces new tournament Ultimate Madness — https://allhiphop.com/news/raps-ultimate-rap-league-just-snapped-ultimate-madness/\n- AllHipHop: Smack Is Back — URL Homecoming — https://allhiphop.com/news/smack-is-back-url-returns-big-stage-battle-rap-to-the-big-apple-with-homecoming/\n- Ultimate Rap League — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ultimate_Rap_League",
