    "body": "Some retros you argue about. The 'Flint' isn't one of them. The Air Jordan 13 'Flint' is back August 1 at $215, and it's one of the most agreed-upon 13s in the whole catalog.\n\n## The colorway\n'Flint' runs Navy with Flint Grey, White and a University Blue hit. It's calm where it needs to be and cold where it counts — the kind of navy that works nine months out of the year. On the 13, a shape built off the movement of a panther, that deep blue makes the whole thing look expensive.\n\n## Why 'Flint' hits different\nThis colorway carries history — it's an OG many heads consider a must-own. When a retro has that kind of standing, the release isn't about hype cycles, it's about restock energy: people who missed it before, plus a new wave that only knows it by reputation. Demand runs steady, not spiky.\n\n## The 13's quiet luxury\nThe 13 is one of the more slept-on Jordans until you have a pair on. The holographic 'eye,' the paw-print sole, the suede — it's a premium build that photographs plain and wears rich. 'Flint' plays right into that: understated in a thumbnail, standout in person.\n\n## Sources\n- Just Fresh Kicks: Air Jordan release dates — https://justfreshkicks.com/air-jordan-release-dates/\n- Sneaker Bar Detroit: Air Jordan release dates 2026 — https://sneakerbardetroit.com/air-jordan-release-dates/\n- House of Heat: Jordan release dates — https://houseofheat.co/jordan-release-dates",
