    "body": "House rule: Cyberpunk always gets a beat, placed by medium. Today it runs anime-side — and the fresh hook isn't the crew, it's the music and the first look.\n\n## The new hook\nThe latest trailer carries an original song — 'You Can't Run From Me' by Rico Nasty, written exclusively for the show and now streaming everywhere. The first Edgerunners lived and died on its needle-drops; putting a Rico Nasty original on the sequel is a statement about the energy they're chasing. That's the new detail worth leading on.\n\n## Fall 2026, on Netflix\nEdgerunners 2 is set for a Fall 2026 release window on Netflix — expect it somewhere between September and November, no exact date locked yet. It's a standalone 10-episode story, described as a raw chronicle of redemption and revenge, following an entirely new cast through Night City's darkest corners.\n\n## The Anime Expo screening\nAt Anime Expo 2026, CD Projekt Red screened the premiere episode — not recorded, not streamed, in the room only. The panel brought showrunner Bartosz Sztybor, EP Saya Elder, director Kai Ikarashi and voice actor Nazeeh Tarsha. Early word out of that room is what's got the fixture buzzing again.\n\n## Why it's placed here\nCyberpunk shows up every episode; the only question is which pillar. A card game or a game update goes to gaming — an anime season goes here. Leading with the Rico Nasty track keeps it fresh instead of re-running the crew reveal. Same fixture, new angle, by the rules.\n\n## Sources\n- Crunchyroll: Edgerunners 2 Fall 2026 release window and visual — https://www.crunchyroll.com/news/latest/2026/6/28/cyberpunk-edgerunners-season-2-fall-2026-release-date-visual\n- CD PROJEKT RED: Edgerunners 2 new trailer and Fall 2026 window — https://press.cdprojektred.com/en/news/1831/cyberpunk-edgerunners-2-gets-new-trailer-and-fall-2026-release-window\n- Popverse: Edgerunners 2 tease at Anime Expo — https://www.thepopverse.com/tv-anime-cyberpunk-edgerunners-2-announcement-coming-july-2026-anime-expo",
