    "heroCredit": "Synthtopia — Polyend Drums at Superbooth 2026",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.synthtopia.com/content/2026/05/07/polyend-drums-debuts-at-superbooth-2026/",
    "body": "Every episode carries a gear beat because the beats are the business, and this week the gear is a statement piece: Polyend Drums.\n\n## What it actually is\nIt's an 8-track hybrid drum machine in an aluminum chassis, and the split is the whole idea. Four tracks are true analog, built on SSI chips — two oscillators each, a noise source, a multimode filter, an envelope-driven amp, plus a digital oscillator on top for layering or FM. The other four tracks are digital, pulling from 40-plus instruments with sub-mode mutations that push the practical sound count into the hundreds. Samples load and layer alongside either engine. So you can build a kick that's genuinely analog and sit it next to a sampled break without leaving the box.\n\n## The part producers will feel\nEffects run in three chains — send, insert, master — and the insert effects are sequenceable per step. That means the effect becomes part of the pattern instead of a coat of paint at mixdown. Add an X/Y fader for real-time morphing and a deep eight-track sequencer with generative tools, and you've got a machine built for performing a beat, not just programming one. Polyend and the press are openly framing it as a rival to Roland's TR-1000, which tells you the lane it's parked in.\n\n## The catch\nIt's $2,699, with pre-orders open on a refundable $500 deposit, in black or silver. That's grown-producer money, not first-drum-machine money. But if you make rhythm for a living, a box that does real analog, digital and sampling with step-sequenced effects is the kind of tool that pays for itself in the sounds nobody else has.\n\n## Tie it home\nYou don't need a $2,699 box to make heat — you need the right loop. That's the whole point of the $79 vault: unlimited beats, instant, so the idea's not waiting on the gear budget.\n\n## Sources\n- Synthtopia: Polyend Drums debuts at Superbooth 2026 — https://www.synthtopia.com/content/2026/05/07/polyend-drums-debuts-at-superbooth-2026/\n- We Rave You: Polyend announces Drums, a $2,699 analog + digital drum machine — https://weraveyou.com/2026/05/polyend-drums-hybrid-drum-machine-superbooth-2026/\n- MusicTech: Polyend unveils Drums — https://musictech.com/news/gear/polyend-drums/",
    "publishedAt": "2026-07-22",
    "goLiveAt": "2026-07-28T17:47:25.582Z"
