    "headline": "The Ghost\nMight Ride Again.",
    "subhead": "Sucker Punch just told fans a single-player story expansion for Yotei isn't off the table — music to a solo-RPG head's ears.",
    "description": "Sucker Punch hasn't ruled out a story DLC for Ghost of Yotei, saying it's in a 'listening phase' after shipping the free Legends co-op mode in March 2026.",
    "keywords": [
      "Ghost of Yotei story expansion",
      "Ghost of Yotei DLC 2026",
      "Ghost of Yotei single player DLC",
      "Sucker Punch Yotei",
      "Ghost of Yotei Legends",
      "Sneakz and Beatz",
      "PHRHX"
    ],
    "ogHeadline": "The ghost\nmight ride again.",
    "ogAccent": "1E1E1E",
    "heroCredit": "PlayStation.Blog — Ghost of Yotei Legends",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://blog.playstation.com/2025/08/19/ghost-of-yotei-legends-dlc-is-coming-in-2026/",
    "body": "Gaming leads in the host's lane — big-world, single-player, story-forward — and Ghost of Yotei just gave that lane something to watch.\n\n## What was said\nCo-director Jason Connell said Sucker Punch hasn't ruled out a story DLC for Ghost of Yotei. They're not promising it, and they're not dating it — the phrase was a 'listening phase,' watching what fans actually want before they commit. That's a studio leaving the door open on more single-player, and for anybody who lived in Atsu's version of feudal Japan, that's the update that matters.\n\n## The context\nThis lands after Yotei's free Legends mode dropped in March — the co-op, supernatural-flavored multiplayer where you and up to three others take on giant demonic versions of the Yotei Six. Legends was the flashy free add-on. A story expansion would be the opposite: quiet, solo, more of the grounded open world that made the base game hit. The devs have also said they're eyeing a next project, so a story DLC would be a bridge, not the finale.\n\n## Why it's the lead\nThis is peak host taste — a samurai open-world built for one player and a long, deliberate story, from the studio that made Tsushima. Even a maybe on more single-player Yotei outranks most of what's shipping, because it's exactly the kind of game the show is built around. Read it straight, though: it's a 'not ruled out,' not an announcement. Mark it a maybe and keep it moving.\n\n## Sources\n- DLCompare: Sucker Punch hints at a new Ghost of Yotei story expansion — https://www.dlcompare.com/gaming-news/ghost-of-yotei-could-be-expanded-with-a-story-dlc-in-the-future\n- PlayStation.Blog: Ghost of Yotei Legends DLC is coming in 2026 — https://blog.playstation.com/2025/08/19/ghost-of-yotei-legends-dlc-is-coming-in-2026/\n- GamingBible: Ghost of Yotei devs eye sequel project, free DLC first — https://www.gamingbible.com/news/platform/playstation/ghost-of-yotei-devs-sequel-project-free-dlc-957319-20260103",
    "publishedAt": "2026-07-22",
    "goLiveAt": "2026-07-28T17:47:27.582Z"
