    "slug": "cyberpunk-project-orion-first-person-2026",
    "pillar": "gaming",
    "title": "Cyberpunk 2 (Project Orion) Locks First-Person",
    "headline": "Night City,\nYour Eyes Only.",
    "subhead": "Cyberpunk's standing beat, game-side: the sequel is staying fully first-person for 'maximum immersion' — and a job listing hints at mobile.",
    "description": "CD Projekt's Cyberpunk sequel Project Orion will keep all story presentation in first-person for immersion, creative director Igor Sarzynski says — with a mobile-platform rumor to watch.",
    "keywords": [
      "Cyberpunk 2 Project Orion",
      "Project Orion first person",
      "Cyberpunk sequel 2026 news",
      "Igor Sarzynski Cyberpunk",
      "Cyberpunk Orion mobile",
      "Sneakz and Beatz",
      "PHRHX"
    ],
    "ogHeadline": "Night City,\nyour eyes only.",
    "ogAccent": "C8901E",
    "heroCredit": "VGTimes — Cyberpunk 2 news (July 2026)",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://vgtimes.com/games/cyberpunk-2/news/",
    "body": "House rule: Cyberpunk always gets a beat, placed by medium. Edgerunners covered the anime side already, so tonight the fixture goes game-side — to Project Orion, the Cyberpunk sequel.\n\n## The fresh design call\nCreative director Igor Sarzynski said the sequel is keeping all story presentation in first-person, on purpose, for maximum immersion and narrative consistency. That settles a real question — after 2077, some expected a camera pull-back for a sequel. CDPR's answer is no: you stay behind the eyes the whole way. For a game whose whole pitch is being inside Night City, committing fully to first-person is a statement about what kind of RPG this is.\n\n## The rumor to flag\nHere's the maybe: a job listing for a Technical QA Lead named mobile devices among target platforms. Read that carefully — it's a hint, not an announcement, that Cyberpunk could stretch toward mobile someday. Treat it as a rumor until CDPR says otherwise. It's the kind of listing that sparks a hundred headlines and confirms nothing.\n\n## The timeline, straight\nOrion's in pre-production, built in Unreal Engine 5 out of CD Projekt's North American studios. The studio's own math is that pre-production to release runs four to five years on average — which is why nobody serious is promising this before the back half of the decade, possibly 2030 or later. So this is a design-and-direction update, not a date. What's new and worth saying on air: first-person is locked, and the mobile whisper is exactly that — a whisper.\n\n## Sources\n- VGTimes: Cyberpunk 2 news and rumors (July 2026) — https://vgtimes.com/games/cyberpunk-2/news/\n- Cyberpunk 2 — Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cyberpunk_2",
