    "slug": "mushoku-tensei-season-3-2026",
    "pillar": "anime",
    "title": "Mushoku Tensei Season 3 Is Here",
    "headline": "The Isekai\nStandard Returns.",
    "subhead": "The show that reset the whole isekai bar is back — Season 3 of Mushoku Tensei premiered July 6.",
    "description": "Mushoku Tensei: Jobless Reincarnation Season 3 premiered July 6, 2026, with an early two-episode screening at Anime Expo 2026 on July 2.",
    "keywords": [
      "Mushoku Tensei Season 3",
      "Mushoku Tensei S3 release date",
      "Jobless Reincarnation season 3",
      "Mushoku Tensei 2026",
      "isekai anime 2026",
      "Sneakz and Beatz",
      "PHRHX"
    ],
    "ogHeadline": "The isekai\nstandard returns.",
    "ogAccent": "2E2E2E",
    "heroCredit": "Anime Expo 2026 — Mushoku Tensei S3 screening",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://comicbook.com/anime/news/anime-expo-2026-every-major-anime-announced/",
    "body": "Staying in the host's wheelhouse — the RPG-flavored isekai lane — Mushoku Tensei just came back, and it's not a small return.\n\n## The date\nSeason 3 of Mushoku Tensei: Jobless Reincarnation premiered July 6, with an early two-episode screening at Anime Expo 2026 on July 2. It's here now, mid-summer, back on the schedule for the crowd that's been following Rudeus since the beginning.\n\n## Why it carries weight\nMushoku Tensei is the show a lot of people point to as the one that took isekai seriously — the studio-quality animation, the world that actually feels lived-in, the character writing that let the genre grow past its power-fantasy reputation. It's flawed and it knows it, and it's built a devoted audience out of watching a broken man try to become a better one across lifetimes. For a host who loves big-world RPGs, this is the anime that scratches the same itch: a fully realized fantasy world you sink into for the long haul.\n\n## Where it sits\nNot the loudest premiere of the summer, but a marquee for the people who care — and this show's people care hard. Season 3 continuing a story this deliberate is its own event. Jump back in from where you left off; this isn't one to start in the middle.\n\n## Sources\n- ComicBook: Anime Expo 2026 — every major anime announced — https://comicbook.com/anime/news/anime-expo-2026-every-major-anime-announced/\n- Complex: The new anime release guide (July 2026) — https://www.complex.com/pop-culture/a/khal/anime-release-guide",
