    "body": "This is the single biggest game on the planet, and right now the whole thing is riding on a two-minute video nobody's seen yet. That's the power Rockstar holds.\n\n## The trailer nobody can date\nAs of late July, Rockstar hasn't announced a date for a third GTA 6 trailer — every \"date\" bouncing around online is community speculation, not a confirmation. What's real is the pattern: a steady summer marketing beat that has projections pointing at late July through mid-August. When it comes, expect a story-heavy cut leaning on protagonists Lucia and Jason, with looks at the HUD and new locations.\n\n## What's actually locked\nThe release date is November 19, 2026 — Rockstar set that officially back in November 2025. Pre-orders opened June 25 at $79.99 for Standard and $99.99 for Ultimate. So the hype isn't vapor; there's a real ship date and a real checkout page behind it.\n\n## Why the host cares\nThis is a single-player, story-first, big-world open-world game — dead center of the lane this show favors. Whatever you think of the wait, GTA 6 is the tentpole the entire industry is planning its fall around.\n\n## The read\nDon't get played by fake trailer countdowns. Watch Rockstar's own channels and nothing else. The trailer drops when it drops; November 19 is the date that matters.\n\n## Sources\n- Forbes: GTA 6 Trailer 3 latest update — https://www.forbes.com/sites/brianmazique/2026/07/20/grand-theft-auto-6-trailer-3-latest-update-on-the-final-piece-of-the-summer-hype-train/\n- GamesRadar: GTA 6 everything we know — https://www.gamesradar.com/gta-6-guide/\n- TechTimes: GTA 6 release date, pre-orders — https://www.techtimes.com/articles/317156/20260525/gta-6-release-date-locked-pre-orders-trailer-3-expected-late-june.htm",
