    "body": "One Piece is the longest-running story in the room, and right now it's in the part fans waited literal years to see animated.\n\n## Where the arc is\nThe first cour of the Elbaf arc concluded on July 5, 2026. The second cour has since picked back up, with new episodes rolling out on Netflix and Crunchyroll on their usual schedule. Elbaf — the land of the giants — is a payoff destination the manga built toward for a very long time, and the anime's finally there.\n\n## Why Elbaf hits different\nThis isn't filler between big fights. Elbaf ties back to threads Eiichiro Oda planted arcs and arcs ago, the kind of long-game setup that made One Piece the standard for serialized storytelling. Seeing it move in animation — color, sound, the scale of the giants — is the reason people who \"fell behind\" are jumping back in.\n\n## The wider moment\nOda's already teased the next arc after Elbaf for 2026, so the story's momentum isn't slowing. For a show that's run since 1999, that pace of payoff is almost unheard of. If you dropped off somewhere in the last decade, Elbaf is a clean, high-stakes place to re-enter.\n\n## The read\nBig name, real payoff, moving now. That's the whole case. The giants' island is exactly where One Piece earns its reputation — press play and catch the wave while it's cresting.\n\n## Sources\n- GamesRadar: One Piece Elbaf arc release schedule — https://www.gamesradar.com/entertainment/anime-shows/one-piece-elbaph-arc-release-date-time-schedule-crunchyroll-netflix/\n- What's on Netflix: One Piece Elbaf Arc Part 2 release date — https://www.whats-on-netflix.com/news/anime/one-piece-elbaf-arc-part-2-netflix-release-date/\n- ComicBook: One Piece confirms full Elbaph schedule for 2026 — https://comicbook.com/anime/news/one-piece-confirms-the-full-elbaph-schedule-for-2026/",
