    "subhead": "Erica Synths and Richie Hawtin's long-teased beat machine landed at Superbooth 2026 - 909-style sequencing, seven-track sampling and modular hookups in one deep little box.",
    "description": "Erica Synths x Richie Hawtin Bullfrog Drums landed at Superbooth 2026 - 909-style sequencing, 7-track sampling and modular hookups in one groovebox.",
    "keywords": [
      "erica synths bullfrog drums",
      "richie hawtin drum machine",
      "bullfrog drums 2026",
      "superbooth 2026 groovebox",
      "909 style sequencer",
      "sampling drum machine 2026",
      "beatmaker gear 2026",
      "producer gear 2026"
    ],
    "ogHeadline": "909 sequencing,\nreal sampling.",
    "ogAccent": "2F5D46",
    "heroCredit": "Erica Synths - Bullfrog Drums (Superbooth 2026)",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://musictech.com/news/gear/richie-hawtin-erica-synths-bullfrog-drums/",
    "body": "Every episode carries a gear beat because gear is the beat business. This week the box people were teasing for two years finally showed up for real.\n\n## What it is\nErica Synths teamed with Richie Hawtin on Bullfrog Drums, and after a 2024 tease it fully materialized at Superbooth 2026. It's built as an educational beat machine, but don't let that word fool you - it blends 909-style sequencing, seven-track sampling and modular connectivity into one surprisingly deep groovebox. Learn on it, then keep making records with it.\n\n## Why the mix matters for beatmakers\n909-style sequencing means the workflow producers already know in their hands - swing, accents, that classic step feel. Seven tracks of sampling means you're not stuck with presets; drop your own drums, your own chops, your own textures. Put those together and you've got a box that teaches the fundamentals and still cooks a real pattern.\n\n## The modular angle\nThe modular connectivity is the part that gives it a long life. Sync it, patch it, let it talk to a rack or another box. That's the difference between a starter toy and something that stays on the desk after you level up. For a producer building a hardware setup piece by piece, a groovebox that plays nice with everything else is worth more than one that lives on an island.\n\n## Ties to the vault\nThis is the same energy behind the $79 beat vault - character in the sound, tools that respect the craft, no laptop babysitting required. If you cop the vault to build out your catalog, a box like Bullfrog is how you start flipping your own from scratch.\n\n## Sources\n- MusicTech: Richie Hawtin x Erica Synths Bullfrog Drums - https://musictech.com/news/gear/richie-hawtin-erica-synths-bullfrog-drums/\n- MusicRadar: Superbooth 2026 gear roundup - https://www.musicradar.com/music-tech/i-went-to-superbooth-and-these-are-the-10-bits-of-gear-i-wanted-to-take-home-with-me\n- Gearnews: Superbooth 2026 synth trends - https://www.gearnews.com/synth-trends-of-superbooth-2026-synth/",
