    "ogHeadline": "Summer madness,\nstacked.",
    "ogAccent": "1C2B45",
    "heroCredit": "Ultimate Rap League (URLtv)",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCflIAeM03JFL9ml03LwYF-g",
    "body": "Battle rap breaks on Twitter/X before it breaks anywhere else, and this week the timeline's on one card: URL's Summer Madness 15.\n\n## The matchup that's moving\nURL slotted Geechi Gotti against Shotty Horroh as one of the headline pairings on the card. Gotti's one of the most decorated names in the modern era - a Compton battler who turned consistency into a resume nobody argues with. Him on the biggest stage in the sport is exactly the kind of booking that gets the timeline talking.\n\n## It's a full card, not a one-off\nSummer Madness is URL's flagship event, and the rest of the lineup backs that up: T-Top vs A.Ward and Loaded Lux vs Nu Jerzey Twork round it out. That's veterans and pillars on one night - the range of styles that makes the event feel like a main card instead of a single fight.\n\n## Why the ownership matters\nURL - the Ultimate Rap League - is Black-owned and still the biggest platform in battle rap. That's the whole point of covering it here. When the sport's marquee night answers to the culture instead of a label, the culture stays in control of its own stage. That's rare, and it's worth saying out loud every time.\n\n## Real talk before you book it\nCards move. Matchups get added, swapped and shuffled right up to showtime, and rumors move faster than official word. Before anybody names a final lineup or a date on air, check URL's official channels - this is a spotlight on what's announced, not a locked bill.\n\n## Sources\n- Ultimate Rap League (URLtv) - https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCflIAeM03JFL9ml03LwYF-g\n- VerseTracker: Summer Madness 15 - https://versetracker.com/events/url-ultimate-rap-league-summer-madness-15\n- VerseTracker: Geechi Gotti - https://versetracker.com/rapper/geechi-gotti",
