    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/",
    "body": "We flagged this one as it approached - now it's here. Today's the premiere, so it earns a slot on its own day.\n\n## What's dropping\nBleach: Thousand-Year Blood War - \"The Calamity\" premieres July 25 as the final cour of the series. It runs thirteen episodes and closes out the story that this TYBW run kicked off back in 2022. Four years of buildup, and the last stretch starts today.\n\n## Why it's a big deal\nBleach's return was one of the great comeback stories in modern anime. The original series ended without ever animating this arc, and fans waited more than a decade. When TYBW finally started, it came back with a budget and a polish the show never had the first time - and it turned a long-suffering fanbase back into an event audience. \"The Calamity\" is where all of that pays off.\n\n## What to expect\nThis is the endgame, so expect the arc's biggest confrontations to land here - the payoffs the manga readers have been holding over everyone else's heads. For the anime-only crowd, it's the finish line for a story that's been building since 2022. Thirteen episodes is a tight, deliberate run to close it clean.\n\n## The honest framing\nThis is a premiere-day note, not a review - it starts today, so the takes will come as it airs. If you fell off during the wait, this is the moment to get current. The show that came back from the dead is about to take its last swing. Confirm your region's streaming platform and drop time before you plan the watch.\n\n## Sources\n- Anime News Network: Main feed July 2026 - https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/main-feed/2026/07\n- Complex: New Anime Release Guide (July 2026) - https://www.complex.com/pop-culture/a/khal/anime-release-guide\n- Crunchyroll: Bleach Thousand-Year Blood War - https://www.crunchyroll.com/series/bleach-thousand-year-blood-war",
