    "ogAccent": "2E2E2E",
    "heroCredit": "Ye Live Concert Tour",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ye_Live_Concert_Tour",
    "publishedAt": "2026-07-26",
    "body": "We open on the GOAT, like every episode. The story today isn't a new city on the map — it's the one with the most weight. Ye's coming home.\n\n## Chicago, back-to-back\nYe's website added a pair of hometown shows — Soldier Field, September 3 and 4 — alongside a July 4 date at the Alamodome in San Antonio. Two nights in the city that made him, on a stadium field, not an arena floor. For a run this size, the hometown stop is the one that reads different.\n\n## It sits on top of a full US leg\nThe Chicago add isn't alone. The US stretch already locked the Caesars Superdome in New Orleans for August 28, and the tour site has been showing a growing board of American stadium dates. After the European leg and a festival stop in Italy, the run turned domestic and started stacking rooms.\n\n## The road here took a fight\nGetting to a US stadium run wasn't clean. Across the summer, several European shows were pulled, and a UK festival booking fell through after his ETA was withdrawn — fallout tied to past antisemitic statements he has since apologized for. State that plainly and leave it neutral. The point for the calendar: the tour rerouted and pointed at America's biggest rooms.\n\n## The album's still in the room\nBully dropped March 28, and a deluxe edition added records in June. A stadium run with a project still in rotation is how you keep something alive for months instead of a weekend — the music and the tour pulling the same way.\n\n## The takeaway\nFor the host, Ye's the greatest to ever do it, and a two-night Soldier Field homecoming is the kind of stamp that outlasts the tour. Banned in some countries, booking his own hometown twice in a row in others. Before you quote a date or a price on air, check his official site — stadium routing moves fast.\n\n## Sources\n- Billboard: Kanye West's Summer Tour Adds Chicago & San Antonio Shows - https://www.billboard.com/music/rb-hip-hop/kanye-west-summer-tour-adds-chicago-san-antonio-shows-1236272815/\n- IQ Magazine: Kanye West adds US shows to ongoing run - https://www.iqmagazine.com/2026/06/tour-news-kanye-west-adds-us-shows-to-ongoing-run/\n- Fox8: Ye bringing 2026 tour to Caesars Superdome in New Orleans - https://www.fox8live.com/2026/07/09/ye-bringing-2026-tour-caesars-superdome-new-orleans/\n- Ye Live Concert Tour - https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ye_Live_Concert_Tour",
