    "body": "August is one of the most stacked Jordan months of the year, and most of it is general-release stuff the whole house can cop. The 8 'BIN 23' is the opposite play — and that's the point.\n\n## What's dropping\nThe Air Jordan 8 'BIN 23' is Jordan Brand's ultra-premium entry, limited to 2,300 individually numbered pairs at $355 retail, releasing August 15. Not a restock, not a family-sizing GR — a capped, numbered run priced like a statement.\n\n## Why the number matters\nTwenty-three hundred pairs, each stamped with its own number, turns a shoe into a ledger. You're not just buying the 8; you're buying a specific position in a run that can't be reprinted at that count. That's what the luxury tier sells — scarcity you can point to, not just a colorway.\n\n## The 8 is an underrated canvas\nThe Jordan 8 doesn't get the 1-and-4 spotlight, but it's got the straps, the fuzzy tongue, the heavy build — a silhouette with enough going on to carry a premium treatment without looking plain. Putting the luxury program on the 8 instead of an obvious model is a flex in itself.\n\n## Where it sits in August\nContext matters: the same month runs the AJ13 'Flint' on the 1st and the AJ6 'Oreo' on the 8th, both wide-release grails. The 'BIN 23' is the collector's counterweight in a month otherwise built for volume. Different buyer, different intent.\n\n## The takeaway\nJordan retros only, and this is the rare one you flex, not beat up. If numbered exclusivity is your lane, August 15 is the date — but confirm the exact SKU and the numbering claim before you treat any of it as locked.\n\n## Sources\n- Men's Journal: Every Air Jordan Releasing in August of 2026 - https://www.mensjournal.com/style/air-jordan-release-date-calendar-august-of-2026\n- Sneaker Bar Detroit: Air Jordan Retro 2026 Release Dates - https://sneakerbardetroit.com/air-jordan-retro-spring-2026-release-dates/"
