    "body": "Some anime news is niche. This isn't. Demon Slayer is one of the few titles that pulls people who don't even watch anime, and the biggest chapter of it just got a streaming date.\n\n## The date\nThe Infinity Castle arc lands on Crunchyroll on July 28 — its first stream after the theatrical run that packed rooms worldwide. If you missed it in a seat, you're two days out from watching it at home.\n\n## Why Infinity Castle is the one\nThis is the arc the whole series was building toward — the final act, the descent into the demon fortress, the fights fans have been reading and waiting on for years. Taking it theatrical first and then to streaming is how you turn a season finale into an event. The box office already proved the demand; the stream cashes it in.\n\n## Streaming beats the wait\nGetting it on Crunchyroll matters because it drops the barrier — no ticket, no showtime, just press play. For a title this big, wide streaming access is what turns a moment into a rewatch, and it puts the arc in front of everyone who couldn't make the theater run.\n\n## Big-name only, and this clears the bar\nThe show only covers anime that's genuinely moving the culture, and Demon Slayer sits at the very top of that list. This isn't a small sequel or a niche premiere — it's the season's headline, full stop.\n\n## The takeaway\nThe movie everybody lined up for is home Tuesday. Whether you're catching up or running it back, July 28 is the date. Confirm the exact regional availability on Crunchyroll before you promise anyone a specific country's stream.\n\n## Sources\n- ComicBook: Anime Expo 2026 - Every Major Anime Announced - https://comicbook.com/anime/news/anime-expo-2026-every-major-anime-announced/\n- ComicBook: 6 New Anime Coming to Hulu in July 2026 - https://comicbook.com/anime/list/6-new-anime-coming-to-hulu-in-july-2026/",
