    "publishedAt": "2026-07-26",
    "body": "Comebacks hit different in anime, where a long gap can either kill momentum or turn a return into an event. Black Clover's betting on the second one.\n\n## The return date\nBlack Clover is set to debut its second season in October 2026 — roughly five years after the first run wrapped. That's a long time to sit on a bench for a title that was pulling big numbers, and the fanbase noticed the moment the window got confirmed.\n\n## Why the gap is the story\nFive years is the headline, not a footnote. Long hiatuses test whether an audience sticks around, and Black Clover's is one of the more anticipated returns on the board — the kind of gap that builds appetite instead of killing it. Leading with the comeback, not the plot, is the right read.\n\n## It anchors a loaded fall\nOctober's shaping up crowded, and Black Clover slots in as one of the loudest names in it. A shonen with this much built-in audience returning in the same window as the rest of the fall slate makes for a real fight for attention — good for fans, tough for everything releasing next to it.\n\n## The underdog energy still fits\nBlack Clover's whole thing is the kid with no magic outworking everybody. A series that spent five years off the air coming back swinging is on-brand for exactly that. The story and the situation rhyme.\n\n## The takeaway\nThe underdog shonen refuses to stay done. If you fell off during the wait, October's the reset. Confirm the exact debut date and platform before you circle it — a window can tighten or move.\n\n## Sources\n- ComicBook: Anime Expo 2026 - Every Major Anime Announced - https://comicbook.com/anime/news/anime-expo-2026-every-major-anime-announced/\n- Gizmodo: The Biggest Announcements From Anime Expo 2026 - https://gizmodo.com/anime-expo-2026-news-announcements-trailers-2000781574",
