    "ogHeadline": "Night City,\nand then some.",
    "ogAccent": "1A4C6E",
    "heroCredit": "NoobFeed",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.noobfeed.com/news/cyberpunk-2-breakthrough-project-orion-leaks",
    "publishedAt": "2026-07-26",
    "body": "Cyberpunk always gets a beat on this show. This cycle it's the sequel — codenamed Project Orion — and a fresh round of leaks that read like ambition turned all the way up. Keep the label on it: leaks, not gospel.\n\n## What the leaks claim\nReports around Project Orion point to CD Projekt Red building the sequel on Unreal Engine 5, leaving the old REDengine behind. The documentation that's circulated suggests a playstyle system that changes as the story moves through major arcs — infiltration, street fighting, engineering, netrunning — with factions reacting to how you build your legend.\n\n## A second city\nThe most eye-catching piece: Cyberpunk creator Mike Pondsmith has described the setting as Night City plus another city that \"feels like Chicago gone wrong.\" A sequel that expands past Night City into a second location is a real scope jump from 2077, and it's the detail fans keep latching onto.\n\n## Where it actually stands\nHere's the sober part. Orion entered pre-production in 2025 and \"Cyberpunk 2\" is still a placeholder title. Analyst estimates put the release somewhere around 2030. So everything above is early — a mix of official comments and leaks, not a shipped feature list. Treat it as direction, not a spec sheet, and say \"reportedly\" on air.\n\n## Why it's the Cyberpunk beat this cycle\nThe standing rule: Cyberpunk news gets placed by medium — game news sits in gaming, Edgerunners sits in anime. This is the game, so it lands here. And it fits the host's lane cleanly: a big-world, single-player RPG built for immersion.\n\n## The takeaway\nNight City plus a second town gone bad, on a new engine, years out — the ambition leaked loud. Just keep the rumor tag on it until CDPR confirms, because a lot can change between pre-production and 2030.\n\n## Sources\n- NoobFeed: Cyberpunk 2 Breakthrough - Project Orion Leaks - https://www.noobfeed.com/news/cyberpunk-2-breakthrough-project-orion-leaks\n- VGTimes: Cyberpunk 2 news - latest news and rumors (July 2026) - https://vgtimes.com/games/cyberpunk-2/news/\n- Notebookcheck: Development of Cyberpunk 2 Project Orion picks up speed - https://www.notebookcheck.net/Development-of-Cyberpunk-2-Project-Orion-picks-up-speed-development-team-strengthened-by-new-high-caliber-additions.801590.0.html",
