    "publishedAt": "2026-07-27",
    "body": "There's the whole industry, and then there's this. GTA 6 has a hard date now — November 19, 2026, on PS5 and Xbox Series X|S — and everything else on the calendar has to move around it.\n\nFor the host, this is the lead. Big world, single player, the kind of game you disappear into for a year. That's the lane.\n\n## The date is real this time\nTake-Two's leadership has said flat out the game won't slip again, and Rockstar has held November 19, 2026 as the launch. After one delay, a confirmed date carries weight — this isn't a window, it's a day.\n\n## Pre-orders opened the floodgates\nPre-orders went live June 25, and Rockstar dropped cover art plus a batch of roughly 60 new screenshots the same stretch. Vice City in daylight, at night, in the swamp — the marketing machine finally turned on.\n\n## Trailer 3 is the last piece\nThere's no official date for Trailer 3, but every sign points to late summer — industry watchers tie it to the run into launch and Take-Two's August earnings call. Expect gameplay this time, not just a mood reel. When it lands, it breaks the internet for a day.\n\n## Why it matters to this show\nGTA moves culture the way an album does — the radio, the fits, the slang, the memes. A new one every decade-plus is a cultural reset, and the 25-45 crowd grew up inside these games. This is the one everybody circles.\n\nMark the calendar. November 19. Then clear your schedule.\n\n## Sources\n- Rockstar Games — GTA VI (rockstargames.com/VI)\n- Forbes — GTA 6 Trailer 3 latest update (July 20, 2026)\n- Vice — Take-Two CEO confirms GTA 6 won't be delayed again",
