    "body": "We open on the GOAT, like always. The story today isn't another US dome — it's the nearest date on the whole board, and it's in Madrid.\n\n## Metropolitano, July 30\nYe is set for the Riyadh Air Metropolitano — Atletico Madrid's stadium — on July 30, billed as a standalone show and his only concert in Spain this cycle. Fans there get Bully material in a room built for 70,000. One night, one city, no second chance to catch it local.\n\n## It sits inside a bigger run\nThis isn't a one-off. The Bully tour has been stacking stadiums, and the US leg already locked a Caesars Superdome date in New Orleans on the way to a full American stretch. Madrid is the near-term stop before the tour turns fully domestic.\n\n## The road here wasn't clean\nGetting a run this size on the calendar took some fallout — several European bookings were pulled across the summer, tied to past antisemitic statements he has since apologized for. State it plainly, leave it neutral. The calendar point stands: the tour kept moving and kept selling rooms.\n\n## Why this one hits\nA standalone stadium night in a city that isn't home, for an artist who's been through the wringer publicly — that's a flex measured in demand, not headlines. If you're anywhere near Spain July 30, that's the ticket.\n\n## Sources\n- esMadrid — Kanye West / Ye at Riyadh Air Metropolitano Stadium\n- Wikipedia — Ye Live Concert Tour\n- Fox8 — Ye bringing 2026 tour to Caesars Superdome, New Orleans",
