    "body": "Battle rap is a standing beat here, and we pull it straight off X — where the battlers actually live. This week the timeline's on a linkup that matters.\n\n## URL meets Queen of the Ring\nThe Ultimate Rap League — the biggest Black-owned platform in the sport — is joining forces with Queen of the Ring, the flagship women's league, for a card billed as 'Royalty.' Two Black-owned houses on one stage, with the women's roster getting URL-level production and reach. (Treat the exact date as still firming up — it surfaced through VerseTracker and the community.)\n\n## Why women's battle rap needs this\nQOTR has carried women's battle rap for over a decade, building stars while the mainstream barely looked. A URL co-sign puts that talent in front of the sport's biggest audience — not a side room, the main one. That's the difference between a scene and a stage.\n\n## The culture-first read\nOur whole mission is showing love to hip-hop in more places than the charts reach — underground, gear, and battle rap included. A women's marquee night is that mission in motion. The bars have always been there; now the platform matches them.\n\n## Watch the timeline\nCards move fast and get announced faster on X. Follow the leagues direct, because by the time it hits an aggregator, the real ones already knew.\n\n## Sources\n- VerseTracker — URL x QOTR 'Royalty' event listing\n- Rap Grid — Queen of the Ring league profile",
