    "body": "Cyberpunk always gets a beat on this show. When the medium's anime, it lands here — and this week the news is a hard date.\n\n## From 'fall' to September 8\nEdgerunners 2 locked its premiere: the pilot hits Netflix September 8, 2026. That's the new part — the window used to just say 'fall,' and now it's a day on the calendar, backed by a fresh trailer.\n\n## Trigger and CDPR, back together\nStudio Trigger returns to animate, reuniting with CD Projekt Red. Trigger's the studio that turned the first season into a phenomenon — kinetic action, real emotional gut-punches — and they're running the sequel too.\n\n## A new story, not a retread\nThe season is built as a standalone 10-episode story with four new characters revealed in the trailer. It's not chasing David and Lucy's arc again; it's a fresh crew in the same city, which keeps the door open for anyone who never saw season one.\n\n## Why it still hits the culture\nThe first Edgerunners sent people back into the game in droves and turned its needle-drop into a streaming monster. A dated, trailer-backed sequel is one of fall's biggest anime events — and it keeps Night City in the conversation ahead of everything CDPR's building next.\n\n## Sources\n- GamesRadar — Cyberpunk: Edgerunners season 2 release date, trailer, story\n- Collider — Edgerunners season 2 official trailer + release date",
