    "body": "Kaiju No. 8 is one of the few newer shonen titles that earned its hype fast. It's back this fall — just not the way you'd expect.\n\n## The short\nThe new project is 'Narumi's Week at Work' (also called Narumi's Weekdays), an original short with a main visual out and a fall 2026 release confirmed. Instead of Kafka Hibino, it centers Gen Narumi — the Defense Force's strongest officer.\n\n## Why a side story now\nStudios use shorts like this to keep a property warm between big pushes. With the final arc anime also announced, 'Narumi's Week at Work' is the appetizer — a lower-stakes look at a fan-favorite while the main course gets built.\n\n## Narumi's the right pick\nNarumi's the cocky, insanely strong number-one officer — the kind of character a standalone short can actually carry. Giving him a week in the spotlight is fan service in the best sense: more of the guy people already wanted more of.\n\n## The read\nKaiju No. 8 broke out on clean action and a likable underdog. Stretching the world with a Narumi short before the finale is smart — keep the Defense Force on screen, keep the fanbase fed.\n\n## Sources\n- Anime Corner — Kaiju No. 8 'Narumi's Week at Work' reveals visual, fall 2026\n- Anime News Network — New Kaiju No. 8 short unveils story, staff, fall debut",
