    "body": "Silksong spent years as a running joke about vaporware. Now it's out, it's beloved, and Team Cherry won't stop adding to it.\n\n## The update\nTeam Cherry rolled out a substantial patch positioned as the final major one before the game's expansion, 'Sea of Sorrow.' The update brings new areas, bosses, and tools, and — like the studio's whole approach — it's free to every owner.\n\n## Why 'free' is the flex\nTeam Cherry built its reputation on giving Hollow Knight players free content DLC after DLC. Carrying that into Silksong — a game that already delivered on a legendary wait — is the studio doubling down on goodwill instead of nickel-and-diming a captive audience.\n\n## Sea of Sorrow on the horizon\nThe expansion is coming in 2026, and this patch is the runway. New areas and bosses now, a full expansion next — Hornet's world keeps getting bigger for people who already sank dozens of hours in.\n\n## For the single-player crowd\nThis is exactly the lane the host lives in: a dense, hand-crafted single-player world with no live-service leash. Silksong rewards mastery and curiosity, and it keeps giving reasons to come back.\n\n## Sources\n- Steam News — Hollow Knight: Silksong, Sea of Sorrow patch\n- Nintendo Life — Silksong expansion coming 2026",
