    "ogAccent": "8A1C24",
    "heroCredit": "MAPPA / Crunchyroll",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.crunchyroll.com/",
    "body": "Some shows earn a wait. Jujutsu Kaisen Season 3 is one of them, and as of July 22 it's not a rumor or a date — it's out, worldwide, and it's the Culling Game.\n\n## What just dropped\nMAPPA launched Season 3 on July 22, 2026, and they went straight at the arc readers have been asking about for years. The season adapts the first half of the Culling Game — the nationwide battle royale Kenjaku sets loose across a set of sealed-off colonies, sorcerers forced to rack up points or die. It's the part of the story where the stakes stop being personal and start being structural.\n\n## Why it matters\nThe Culling Game is where Jujutsu Kaisen shifts gears. New players, new rules, a board that keeps moving. It's dense source material, and how MAPPA paces it is the whole ballgame. Season 2 set a bar with Shibuya. This arc has to carry that weight and set up everything after it.\n\n## The move\nYou don't need a countdown for this one. It's live. If you fell off after Shibuya, this is the jump-back-on point — the game just started, and everybody's in it.\n\n## Sources\n- Anime News Network — 2026 news archive: https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2026\n- Crunchyroll: https://www.crunchyroll.com/",
