    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/",
    "body": "Chainsaw Man has never moved like a normal shonen, and its rollout doesn't either. After the Reze Arc got the film treatment, MAPPA lined up the next swing: the Assassins Arc.\n\n## What's confirmed\nThe announcement landed at a MAPPA event and put the Assassins Arc on every timeline overnight. Details are thin — no firm window yet, no full staff breakdown — but the direction is set. Denji's story keeps rolling into one of its wildest stretches.\n\n## Why the culture cares\nThis is the arc that widens the world. New devils, new hunters, and the kind of tonal whiplash — funny one minute, brutal the next — that made the series a phenomenon. Getting it as its own entry, rather than buried in a packed season, says MAPPA knows what it's holding.\n\n## The move\nKeep it on the radar. Chainsaw Man rewards patience, and the announcement alone is enough to reset expectations. When the trailer hits, it'll take over a weekend.\n\n## Sources\n- ComicBook — Chainsaw Man next anime update: https://comicbook.com/anime/news/chainsaw-man-reveals-release-date-for-next-major-anime-update/\n- Anime News Network: https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/",
