    "ogHeadline": "Ye\nShut Out of the UK.",
    "ogAccent": "222222",
    "heroCredit": "Ye Live Concert Tour",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ye_Live_Concert_Tour",
    "body": "The Bully tour has been a story of a comeback that keeps expanding — new markets, new stadiums, a record crowd in Istanbul. This week it hit a wall, and the wall is a border.\n\n## What happened\nThe UK Home Office withdrew Ye's electronic travel authorization, denying him entry to the country. With no way in, his Wireless 2026 headline shows are cancelled. The decision traces back to past antisemitic and Nazi-sympathizing comments he made — remarks he has since apologized for — which have shadowed this run with cancellations and travel restrictions in more than one country.\n\n## The context, straight\nThis isn't a scheduling change or a new date. It's a reversal: a government pulling clearance and a festival losing its headliner. The rest of the tour — the US and European dates — is still standing as of now.\n\n## Why it lands\nYe is one of the most influential artists alive, and his career has always run through controversy and consequence at the same time. You can respect the catalog and still report the facts: the words carried a cost, and the UK just made that cost a locked door.\n\n## Sources\n- Time Out — Wireless 2026 cancelled: https://www.timeout.com/london/news/kanye-west-is-wireless-festival-2026-cancelled-040726\n- IQ Magazine — tour news: https://www.iqmagazine.com/2026/06/tour-news-kanye-west-adds-us-shows-to-ongoing-run/\n- Ye Live Concert Tour: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ye_Live_Concert_Tour",
    "publishedAt": "2026-07-28",
    "goLiveAt": "2026-07-28T17:48:18.582Z"
