    "ogHeadline": "The Witcher 4\nFull Production.",
    "ogAccent": "6E1C1C",
    "heroCredit": "CD Projekt Red",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.pcgamesn.com/the-witcher-4/",
    "body": "The Witcher 4 stopped being a teaser and became a real production this year, and the shape of it is clear: this is Ciri's game.\n\n## Where it stands\nCD Projekt Red confirmed the game entered full production, off the back of a tech demo shown at Unreal Fest 2026 that kicked off the marketing campaign. The studio ramped to a record 933 employees — 220-plus new hires in a year — with the team now focused on finishing the world.\n\n## What we saw\nCiri is the lead, not a side act. The demo showed her casting spells on the move, with next-gen motion capture built to carry real emotion rather than Geralt's stone face. CDPR is also promising smarter NPC routines and a world that reacts harder to your choices, plus a deeper RPG system that changes how you fight.\n\n## The move\nNo date yet, and a game this size won't rush one. But \"full production\" is the milestone that matters — it means the vision is locked and the machine is running. For anyone who lives in single-player open worlds, this is the biggest one on the horizon.\n\n## Sources\n- PCGamesN — The Witcher 4 hub: https://www.pcgamesn.com/the-witcher-4/\n- GameRant — Witcher 4 details: https://gamerant.com/witcher-4-news-details-features/",
