    "body": "The Naruto arm of the Big Three has been dark since 2023. That's about to change.\n\n## What's confirmed\nRevealed through a franchise 10th-anniversary trailer, Studio Pierrot is producing a Boruto: Two Blue Vortex anime — and it's switching from the old weekly grind to a seasonal release model. Pierrot leadership framed the change as a way to ease animator crunch and stop the anime from outrunning the manga, with staff describing an adaptation \"serious\" enough that there's little room for filler.\n\n## Why the model matters\nThe weekly-forever model is what burned out staff and produced the filler slogs fans dreaded. Going seasonal — the structure behind recent Demon Slayer and Jujutsu Kaisen runs — is Pierrot betting that a tighter, better-looking Boruto beats a constant one.\n\n## What's not confirmed\nNo premiere date, no streaming home, no episode count. The manga went on hiatus after Chapter 36 and resumes in V Jump's oversized November issue (on sale Sept 18). Anything sharper than \"expected late 2026 or early 2027\" is fan speculation.\n\n## The read\nNaruto's story is rejoining One Piece and Bleach on air, done the modern way. If the seasonal gamble lands, Boruto stops being the sequel people slept on.\n\n## Sources\n- CBR: https://www.cbr.com/naruto-boruto-two-blue-vortex-anime-trailer/\n- ScreenRant: https://screenrant.com/",
